E["item:99-year-old-port"] = {t="item",n="99-Year-Old Port",z="wailing",s="The 99-Year-Old Port is an exceptionally rare bottle of vintage liquor shipped from Booty Bay as a personal gift for Gazlowe. After a cargo accident on the Ratchet docks, it was snatched away by a lunatic named Mad Magglish, who fled into the twisting tunnels outside the Wailing Caverns.",h="The 99-Year-Old Port is an exceptionally rare bottle of vintage liquor shipped from Booty Bay as a personal...",sec={{t="A High-Value Cargo Spill",b="Transporting precious freight across the Great Sea always carries risks, but Crane Operator Bigglefuzz made things far worse during a routine morning unloading in Ratchet. Attempting to clear an overwhelming shipment from Booty Bay, the goblin overloaded his crane and brought a mountain of crates crashing down onto the docks. In the chaos, the town eccentric—a troublesome figure known as Mad Magglish—snatched an extraordinarily aged bottle of 99-Year-Old Port and bolted into the hills toward the Wailing Caverns.",sp=0},{t="Diplomatic Vintage",b="The stolen port was no ordinary spirits; it was sent by Baron Revilgaz of the Blackwater Raiders as an esteemed diplomatic gift for Gazlowe, the chief engineer and ruler of Ratchet. Losing such a prized consignment threatened Bigglefuzz's livelihood and ratcheted up tensions with the dockmaster. Tracked into the darkened outer grottos of the caverns, the elusive thief lurks in the shadows with the unopened prize, forcing the dockhands to recruit outside mercenaries to retrieve it before Gazlowe discovers the blunder.",sp=1}},faq={{q="Who was the 99-Year-Old Port originally meant for?",a="The bottle was sent by Baron Revilgaz, master of Booty Bay, as a high-value personal gift to Gazlowe, the boss of Ratchet.",al={"who is the port for","who gets the port","gazlowe gift"},it="why_wanted"},{q="How did Mad Magglish end up with the port?",a="Crane Operator Bigglefuzz attempted to unload more cargo than his rig could handle, spilling crates across the Ratchet docks. Mad Magglish took advantage of the mayhem to snatch the vintage bottle and run.",al={"how was it stolen","who stole the port","dock mishap"}},{q="Where did Mad Magglish take the bottle?",a="Magglish fled inland across the Barrens and holed up in the rocky antechambers and outer tunnels leading into the Wailing Caverns.",al={"where is mad magglish","where is the port hidden","port location"},it="place"},{q="Why didn't Bigglefuzz retrieve the port himself?",a="Bigglefuzz pursued the thief to the threshold of the Wailing Caverns, but terrified of the beasts and corrupted druids infesting the caves, he refused to go inside.",al={"why bigglefuzz not chase","crane operator coward"},it="motive"},{q="What is the 99-Year-Old Port?",a="It is an exceptionally rare and aged bottle of fortified wine shipped all the way from Booty Bay. Sent as a prestigious personal gift from Baron Revilgaz to Gazlowe, the chief engineer and leader of Ratchet, this vintage represents an invaluable token of esteem between powerful goblin trade barons.",al={"what is 99-year-old port","99 year old port","bottle of port"},it="identity",add="5b0242c9"}},ang={["class:Rogue"]="Mad Magglish relies on amateur stealth to skulk in the dark outside the Wailing Caverns, but a skilled rogue can easily flush him out of the shadows."},kw={"99-year-old port","bigglefuzz","gazlowe","mad magglish","port","ratchet","revilgaz","wailing caverns"},rel={"quest:959","npc:crane-operator-bigglefuzz","npc:baron-revilgaz","subzone:ratchet","zone:wailing","zone:barrens","subzone:booty-bay"},src={"99-Year-Old Port","Trouble at the Docks"}}
E["item:deviate-hide"] = {t="item",n="Deviate Hide",z="wailing",s="Deviate Hides are the mutated skins stripped from the beasts dwelling within the Wailing Caverns. Warped by the corrupting dream of the druid Naralex, these otherworldly pelts are sought by druids looking to repurpose the nightmare's taint into durable leather goods.",h="Deviate Hides are the mutated skins stripped from the beasts dwelling within the Wailing Caverns.",sec={{t="Tainted Pelts of the Nightmare",b="When the night elf druid Naralex entered his deep slumber beneath the Barrens, his dream turned into an Emerald Nightmare that warped the local cavern ecology. The beasts lurking in the depths transformed into unnatural deviate predators with tough, mutated hides. While inherently touched by evil, these pelts possess unusual, supple resilience that makes them uniquely suited for leathercrafting. Nalpak, perched high above the cavern mouth in the skull-shaped rock formation, collects these hides to study their properties and fashion them into sturdy utility packs.",sp=0}},faq={{q="What makes a deviate hide different from normal leather?",a="Deviate hides come from creatures warped by the Emerald Nightmare seeping out of Naralex's slumber. This corruption alters their flesh, bestowing strange, otherworldly durability and elasticity that ordinary beast pelts lack.",al={"deviate hide lore","why are deviate hides weird","deviate pelt nature"},it="identity"},{q="Who is collecting these hides?",a="Nalpak, a disciple of Naralex camped in the eye-socket cave above the entrance to the Wailing Caverns, seeks these pelts. He believes that despite the wicked nature of the deviate beasts, their materials can be redeemed and fashioned into useful leather goods.",al={"who wants deviate hides","nalpak hides","who needs deviate hide"},it="why_wanted"},{q="Where are deviate hides found?",a="They are taken from the various deviate beasts prowling inside the Wailing Caverns beneath the Barrens, including raptors, vipers, crocolisks, and dreadfangs.",al={"where do deviate hides drop","how to get deviate hides"},it="place",gp=true},{q="Where does Deviate Hide come from, and who made it?",a="Deviate hides are taken from the strange, warped beasts that roam deep within the Wailing Caverns. These creatures were not crafted by mortal hands; rather, they arose from beneath the Barrens, mutated by the foul nightmare that consumed the druid Naralex as he fell into his deep slumber. The unnatural corruption altered the native wildlife, granting their skins strange and otherworldly qualities.",al={"where do deviate hides come from","deviate hide origin","who made deviate hide"},it="origin",add="8b5833f5"}},ang={["class:Druid"]="For druids, collecting deviate hides is a stark confrontation with the Emerald Nightmare's corruptive power over nature, though disciples like Nalpak attempt to redeem the corrupted materials for practical survival."},kw={"barrens","deviate hide","leather","nalpak","naralex","nightmare","pelts","wailing caverns"},rel={"npc:nalpak","quest:1486","zone:wailing","npc:naralex","zone:barrens"},src={"Deviate Hide","Deviate Hides (Classic)"}}
E["item:gem-of-anacondra"] = {t="item",n="Gem of Anacondra",z="wailing",s="The Gem of Anacondra is one of four dream gems held by the corrupted serpent leaders within the Wailing Caverns. Carried by Lady Anacondra, it serves as tangible proof of her defeat and the curbing of the Nightmare's spread over the Barrens.",h="The Gem of Anacondra is one of four dream gems held by the corrupted serpent leaders within the Wailing...",sec={{t="A Corrupted Focus",b="When Naralex entered his deep slumber to bring water and life back to the arid Barrens, the Emerald Nightmare invaded his thoughts and warped his closest disciples. Lady Anacondra and her fellow conspirators abandoned their traditional ways to become the Druids of the Fang, twisting their noble restorative purpose into a toxic delusion. The Gem of Anacondra is one of the four dream gems carried by these serpentine leaders, focusing their corrupted bond with the Emerald Dream and anchoring the nightmare within the cave system.",sp=0},{t="Cleansing the Vision",b="Nara Wildmane and the circle of Cenarion druids in Thunder Bluff found their own slumbers plagued by the visions and wicked faces of the Fang's leadership. Claiming the Gem of Anacondra—alongside the stones of Cobrahn, Pythas, and Serpentis—is necessary to verify that Lady Anacondra has been struck down, lifting the oppressive nightmare from the minds of Kalimdor's balance-keepers.",sp=1}},faq={{q="What is the Gem of Anacondra?",a="It is a dream gem carried by Lady Anacondra, one of the four leaders of the twisted Druids of the Fang residing within the Wailing Caverns.",al={"what is anacondra gem","anacondra gem","what does gem of anacondra do"},it="identity"},{q="Who wants this gem?",a="Nara Wildmane, a tauren druid located on the Elder Rise in Thunder Bluff, seeks the gem along with the other three dream gems to free her mind from nightmares and protect the Barrens.",al={"who takes gem of anacondra","where do i turn in anacondra gem","gem of anacondra turn in"},it="why_wanted"},{q="Where can the Gem of Anacondra be found?",a="The gem is carried by Lady Anacondra, who can be found lurking within the winding subterranean tunnels of the Wailing Caverns in the central Barrens.",al={"where does it drop","who drops gem of anacondra","lady anacondra location"},it="origin",gp=true},{q="Why are the dream gems important?",a="The four gems are held by the corrupt leaders of the Druids of the Fang. Gathering them confirms the ringleaders have been eliminated, breaking their hold over the Emerald Dream's corruption in the region.",al={"why four gems","purpose of dream gems","leaders of the fang gems"},it="power"},{q="Where does the Gem of Anacondra come from, and who made it?",a="The gem is carried by Lady Anacondra deep within the Wailing Caverns. While the exact master who cut or enchanted it is unknown, it serves as one of the dream gems held by the four leaders of the Druids of the Fang. Once part of a noble circle dedicated to healing the Barrens, these corrupted night elves now channel their twisted visions of the Emerald Dream into these stones.",al={"origin gem of anacondra","who made gem of anacondra","where did anacondra get her gem"},it="origin",add="2e0de493"}},ang={["class:Druid"]="For Cenarion druids, claiming this gem is a solemn duty to strike down a sister who surrendered her mind and forms to the corrupting Emerald Nightmare.",["race:Tauren"]="Recovering the gem directly aids Nara Wildmane of Thunder Bluff, lifting the dark visions that plague the slumber of the Shu'halo on the Elder Rise."},kw={"dream gem","druids of the fang","gem of anacondra","lady anacondra","leaders of the fang","nara wildmane","wailing caverns"},rel={"npc:lady-anacondra","quest:914","zone:wailing","topic:druids-of-the-fang","item:gem-of-cobrahn","item:gem-of-pythas","item:gem-of-serpentis","zone:thunderbluff"},src={"Gem of Anacondra","Leaders of the Fang"}}
E["item:gem-of-cobrahn"] = {t="item",n="Gem of Cobrahn",z="wailing",s="The Gem of Cobrahn is a dream gem carried by Lord Cobrahn, one of the corrupt leaders of the Druids of the Fang within the Wailing Caverns. It serves as both a focus of his corrupted reverie and physical proof needed by Nara Wildmane to confirm his defeat.",h="The Gem of Cobrahn is a dream gem carried by Lord Cobrahn, one of the corrupt leaders of the Druids of the...",sec={{t="A Focus of Corrupted Dreams",b="When the night elf druid Naralex entered the Emerald Dream to restore the barren plains of Kalimdor, his nightmare twisted both the Wailing Caverns and his disciples. Among them was Cobrahn, who abandoned the peaceful ways of the Cenarion Circle to take the shape of the serpent. Lord Cobrahn carries one of the four dream gems that anchor the leaders' hold over the subterranean waterways, using it to channel the twisted dreams that threaten to transform the Barrens into a venomous marsh.",sp=0},{t="Restoring Balance",b="In Thunder Bluff, the tauren druid Nara Wildmane is tormented by nightmares sent by the rogue Druids of the Fang. To cleanse the subterranean springs and protect Kalimdor from their vision, adventurers must delve into the caverns, slay Lord Cobrahn alongside his three conspirators, and recover their dream gems. Returning Cobrahn's gem to the Cenarion druids brings an end to his corrupting influence over the slumbering Naralex.",sp=1}},faq={{q="What is the Gem of Cobrahn?",a="It is a dream gem held by Lord Cobrahn, a fallen druid who leads the Druids of the Fang inside the Wailing Caverns. It acts as a conduit for his nightmare-twisted powers.",al={"gem of cobrahn","cobrahn gem","what is cobrahn gem"},it="identity"},{q="Who wants the Gem of Cobrahn?",a="Nara Wildmane, a tauren druid located on the Elder Rise in Thunder Bluff, asks for the gem along with three others to put an end to the Druids of the Fang.",al={"who needs gem of cobrahn","cobrahn gem turn in","who takes cobrahn gem"},it="why_wanted"},{q="How many gems are needed to complete the quest?",a="Four gems are required: the Gem of Cobrahn, the Gem of Anacondra, the Gem of Pythas, and the Gem of Serpentis, each held by one of the four serpent leaders in the caverns.",al={"how many dream gems","leaders of the fang gems","all fang gems"},gp=true},{q="Who is Lord Cobrahn?",a="Lord Cobrahn was once a disciple of Archdruid Naralex. When Naralex's vision turned into a nightmare, Cobrahn and several other druids embraced the form of the serpent and formed the Druids of the Fang.",al={"who is cobrahn","lord cobrahn lore","cobrahn"}}},ang={["class:Druid"]="For Cenarion druids, reclaiming the Gem of Cobrahn marks the tragic but necessary end of a fallen brother who abandoned the harmony of nature for the Emerald Nightmare.",["race:Tauren"]="The druids of Thunder Bluff watch the Barrens closely; taking Cobrahn's gem directly safeguards the plains and hunting grounds from unnatural corruption."},kw={"dream gem","druids of the fang","gem of cobrahn","leaders of the fang","lord cobrahn","nara wildmane","wailing caverns"},rel={"quest:914","npc:lord-cobrahn","topic:druids-of-the-fang","item:gem-of-anacondra","item:gem-of-pythas","item:gem-of-serpentis","zone:wailing","zone:thunderbluff"},src={"Gem of Cobrahn","Leaders of the Fang"}}
E["item:gem-of-pythas"] = {t="item",n="Gem of Pythas",z="wailing",s="The Gem of Pythas is one of four corrupted dream gems carried by the leaders of the Druids of the Fang within the Wailing Caverns. Held by Lord Pythas, it fuels the nightmare twisting the subterranean oasis and threatening the Barrens.",h="The Gem of Pythas is one of four corrupted dream gems carried by the leaders of the Druids of the Fang within...",sec={{t="A Vessel of the Nightmare",b="When Naralex entered the Emerald Dream to restore the arid Barrens, his noble vision was twisted into a living nightmare. His foremost followers fell with him, styling themselves the Druids of the Fang and seeking to remake the surface world into a venomous jungle. Lord Pythas carries this resonant stone, one of four dream gems anchoring the corruption within the caverns. The gem serves as a conduit of their dark design and proof to the druids of Thunder Bluff that Pythas's twisted trance has finally been broken.",sp=0}},faq={{q="What is the Gem of Pythas used for?",a="The gem is brought to Nara Wildmane in Thunder Bluff along with the gems of Cobrahn, Anacondra, and Serpentis. Together, they complete the task of putting an end to the rogue leaders of the Druids of the Fang.",al={"gem of pythas use","what to do with gem of pythas","pythas gem quest"},it="purpose"},{q="Who carries this gem?",a="It is held by Lord Pythas, a fallen night elf druid who resides deep inside the Wailing Caverns of the Barrens.",al={"who drops gem of pythas","pythas location","where to get gem of pythas"},it="target"},{q="Why do the druids of Thunder Bluff want the gem?",a="Nara Wildmane and the Cenarion druids in Thunder Bluff are haunted by the corruption radiating from the Wailing Caverns. Securing the gems proves that the four aberrant leaders have been slain, cutting off the nightmare from bleeding further into the Barrens.",al={"why does nara want gems","nara wildmane pythas"},it="why_wanted"},{q="Are there other gems like this one?",a="Yes. Lord Pythas is one of four leaders. The others—Lady Anacondra, Lord Cobrahn, and Lord Serpentis—each carry their own dream gem deep inside the cavern.",al={"other dream gems","fang gems","wailing caverns gems"},it="ties"},{q="What is the Gem of Pythas?",a="The Gem of Pythas is one of four dream gems carried by the leaders of the Druids of the Fang within the Wailing Caverns. Held by Lord Pythas, this relic embodies the dark, serpentine madness that corrupted these once-noble night elves, binding their twisted visions of the Emerald Dream into physical form.",al={"gem of pythas","what is gem of pythas","what is this gem"},it="identity",add="3d8d64d3"}},ang={["class:Druid"]="For Cenarion druids, recovering the gem is a somber duty, as it represents the utter degradation of Naralex's inner circle into serpentine horrors.",["race:Tauren"]="The twisted rituals in the caverns threaten the fragile balance of the Barrens, making the recovery of these gems critical to protecting the shamans' and druids' homeland."},kw={"barrens","dream gem","druids of the fang","gem of pythas","lord pythas","nara wildmane","wailing caverns"},rel={"npc:lord-pythas","quest:914","zone:wailing","topic:druids-of-the-fang","item:gem-of-cobrahn","item:gem-of-anacondra","item:gem-of-serpentis","zone:thunderbluff"},src={"Gem of Pythas","Leaders of the Fang"}}
E["item:gem-of-serpentis"] = {t="item",n="Gem of Serpentis",z="wailing",s="The Gem of Serpentis is a dream gem carried by Lord Serpentis, the self-proclaimed head of the Druids of the Fang in the Wailing Caverns. It acts as a focal conduit for the twisted nightmare reshaping the cave network and threatening the Barrens.",h="The Gem of Serpentis is a dream gem carried by Lord Serpentis, the self-proclaimed head of the Druids of the...",sec={{t="Heart of the Serpentine Dream",b="When Naralex's slumber inside the Wailing Caverns succumbed to the Emerald Nightmare, his most devoted followers were warped into the fanatical Druids of the Fang. At the pinnacle of this cabal sits Lord Serpentis. Like his three serpentine lieutenants, Serpentis carries an enchanted dream gem that anchors their collective will to the corrupted vision. Recovering this gem breaks Serpentis's hold over the cavern's ecosystem, striking directly at the leadership directing the corruption spreading across the Barrens.",sp=0},{t="Proof for Thunder Bluff",b="The tauren druids atop Thunder Bluff's Elder Rise, particularly Nara Wildmane, endure vivid nightmares caused by the corruption lurking beneath the savannah. Recovering the Gem of Serpentis alongside those of Cobrahn, Anacondra, and Pythas provides tangible proof that the rogue order's ringleaders have fallen, easing the nightmare's grasp on the Cenarion Circle in Mulgore.",sp=1}},faq={{q="Where does the Gem of Serpentis come from?",a="The gem is carried by Lord Serpentis, the leader of the Druids of the Fang, who resides deep inside the winding waterways of the Wailing Caverns.",al={"who drops gem of serpentis","where to get serpentis gem","serpentis gem location"},it="origin"},{q="What is the purpose of the gem?",a="It serves as one of four focus gems used by the leaders of the Druids of the Fang to channel the nightmare warping the subterranean oasis. Nara Wildmane in Thunder Bluff seeks it as proof that Lord Serpentis has been defeated.",al={"why do i need gem of serpentis","what is gem of serpentis for"},it="purpose"},{q="Who wants all four dream gems?",a="Nara Wildmane, a druid stationed on the Elder Rise in Thunder Bluff, asks adventurers to bring her the gems of Cobrahn, Anacondra, Pythas, and Serpentis to sever the nightmare's hold over the region.",al={"who takes the gems","turn in serpentis gem","leaders of the fang turn in"},it="why_wanted"},{q="Who was Lord Serpentis before carrying this gem?",a="He was originally a disciple of Naralex who entered the caverns intending to restore lush life to the Barrens, but the Emerald Nightmare twisted his noble aspirations into a fanatical desire to remake the world in serpent form.",al={"lord serpentis lore","who is serpentis"},it="identity"},{q="What is the Gem of Serpentis?",a="The Gem of Serpentis is one of four dream gems held by the leaders of the Druids of the Fang within the Wailing Caverns. Carried by Lord Serpentis himself, it serves as an emblem and instrument of the corrupted druids who seek to twist the Barrens to match their dark visions.",al={"gem of serpentis lore","what is serpentis gem","lord serpentis gem"},it="identity",add="58ca37b7"}},ang={["class:Druid"]="The dream gems carried by Serpentis and his cabal represent the terrible risk of entering deep trance communion with the Dream without vigilant spiritual discipline.",["race:Tauren"]="Severing Serpentis's hold on this gem helps free the shamans and druids of Thunder Bluff from the dark visions disturbing their sleep across Mulgore."},kw={"druids of the fang","gem of serpentis","leaders of the fang","lord serpentis","nara wildmane","the barrens","wailing caverns"},rel={"npc:lord-serpentis","quest:914","topic:druids-of-the-fang","zone:wailing","quest:1490","item:gem-of-anacondra","item:gem-of-cobrahn","item:gem-of-pythas"},src={"Gem of Serpentis","Leaders of the Fang"}}
E["item:serpentbloom"] = {t="item",n="Serpentbloom",z="wailing",s="Serpentbloom is a rare, subterranean herb found growing only in the dark depths of the Wailing Caverns. Its potent natural properties have drawn the keen interest of the Forsaken's Royal Apothecary Society.",h="Serpentbloom is a rare, subterranean herb found growing only in the dark depths of the Wailing Caverns.",sec={{t="A Rare Subterranean Flora",b="Serpentbloom grows exclusively within the damp, shadowy tunnels of the Wailing Caverns beneath the Barrens. Rooted in an ecosystem warped by unrestrained Emerald Dream energies, the plant thrives far from sunlight and often harbors venomous serpents nesting among its stems. Because the cave system is overrun with hostile beasts and corrupted druids, few who venture inside ever return with viable specimens.",sp=0},{t="Apothecary Interest",b="Operating from the Pools of Vision beneath Thunder Bluff, Apothecary Zamah collects Serpentbloom on behalf of the Royal Apothecary Society of Undercity. The Forsaken continuously seek out virulent, strange, and chemically potent vegetation across Kalimdor to fuel their research for the Dark Lady. Zamah believes that harvesting Serpentbloom in significant quantities could yield valuable breakthroughs for Forsaken alchemy.",sp=0}},faq={{q="Where does Serpentbloom grow?",a="Serpentbloom is found only deep inside the Wailing Caverns, a labyrinthine cavern network located southwest of the Crossroads in the Barrens. It clings to the ground in the dark, damp recesses of the cave.",al={"where to find serpentbloom","serpentbloom location","wailing caverns herb"},it="place",gp=true},{q="Why does the Royal Apothecary Society want Serpentbloom?",a="Apothecary Zamah, an agent of the Royal Apothecary Society stationed in Thunder Bluff, seeks the plant for research. The Forsaken examine unusual and dangerous flora from across Kalimdor to develop new chemical concoctions and support the broader goals of Sylvanas Windrunner.",al={"who wants serpentbloom","apothecary zamah herb","why collect serpentbloom"},it="why_wanted"},{q="Why is harvesting Serpentbloom hazardous?",a="Beyond the general perils of the Wailing Caverns—which crawl with raptors, crocolisks, and corrupted druids—the herb itself frequently shelters venomous snakes. Disturbing the plant often prompts these hidden serpents to strike.",al={"serpentbloom danger","serpentbloom snake"},it="danger",gp=true},{q="Can herbalists find Serpentbloom more easily?",a="Yes. Those trained in herbalism are naturally attuned to spotting vegetative growth and can track Serpentbloom patches amid the shadowy corners of the cavern floor.",al={"find serpentbloom herbalism","tracking serpentbloom"},gp=true},{q="What is Serpentbloom?",a="Serpentbloom is an exceedingly rare specimen of flora native to the darkest recesses of the Wailing Caverns in the Barrens. Rooted within the damp, subterranean depths, this unusual herb is distinguished by its serpent-like qualities—disturbing it often draws out aggressive snakes nestled around its roots.",al={"what is serpentbloom","serpentbloom herb","serpentbloom info"},it="identity",add="bee22cd2"}},ang={["race:Undead"]="Procuring Serpentbloom directly aids Apothecary Zamah and the Royal Apothecary Society as they search foreign lands for botanical assets to strengthen the Forsaken.",["profession:Herbalism"]="Trained herbalists possess the keen eyes necessary to track down these rare cavernous blooms where others see only damp stone."},kw={"apothecary zamah","barrens","herb","royal apothecary society","serpentbloom","thunder bluff","wailing caverns"},rel={"quest:962","quest:853","zone:wailing","zone:barrens","zone:thunderbluff","topic:royal-apothecary-society","topic:forsaken","zone:undercity"},src={"Serpentbloom","Serpentbloom (quest)"}}
E["item:wailing-essence"] = {t="item",n="Wailing Essence",z="wailing",s="Wailing Essence is a strange, concentrated substance found within the ectoplasms roaming deep inside the Wailing Caverns. Suspected of fueling the bizarre mutations spreading through the flora and fauna of the Barrens, it has drawn the attention of opportunistic alchemists eager to bottle its potent properties.",h="Wailing Essence is a strange, concentrated substance found within the ectoplasms roaming deep inside the...",sec={{t="A Volatile Concoction",b="The subterranean caverns beneath the central Barrens have grown thick with unnatural energy, warping beasts and giving rise to gelatinous ectoplasms. These oozing creatures concentrate a viscous substance known as Wailing Essence. While local druids observe these waters with growing dread, goblin entrepreneurs see only raw commercial opportunity. In the port town of Ratchet, an eccentric alchemist named Mebok Mizzyrix believes this essence is the missing active ingredient for a line of lucrative 'smart drinks' meant to enhance consumer intellect, utterly unconcerned with the nightmarish corruption it might actually harbor.",sp=0}},faq={{q="Where does Wailing Essence come from?",a="It is gathered from the ectoplasmic slimes inside the Wailing Caverns, including devouring ectoplasms, evolving ectoplasms, and nightmare ectoplasms.",al={"wailing essence drop","where to get wailing essence","what drops wailing essence"},it="origin"},{q="Who wants this essence?",a="Mebok Mizzyrix, a goblin experimenter located in Ratchet, seeks the essence to brew a new formula of his intellect-boosting 'smart drinks.'",al={"who needs wailing essence","who buys wailing essence","wailing essence turn in"},it="why_wanted"},{q="What is the essence suspected of doing to the Barrens?",a="Mebok suspects that the essence is the root cause behind the rapidly mutating wildlife and unnatural plant overgrowth observed spreading across the Barrens.",al={"what does wailing essence do","is wailing essence dangerous","wailing essence lore"},it="power"},{q="Is drinking Wailing Essence actually safe?",a="Given that it is extracted from corrupt, nightmare-tainted ectoplasms deep in a cursed cavern, consuming it in a commercial beverage is reckless at best, though typical for goblin entrepreneurial standards.",al={"can you drink wailing essence","is smart drink safe"},it="danger"},{q="What is Wailing Essence?",a="Wailing Essence is a strange, potent substance found deep within the Wailing Caverns. It gathers inside the cavern's roaming ectoplasms and oozes, suspected by local observers of being the unnatural catalyst behind the bizarre mutations altering plants and wildlife throughout the surrounding Barrens.",al={"what is wailing essence","wailing essence info","about wailing essence"},it="identity",add="387b8d38"}},ang={["class:Druid"]="The existence of this essence points directly to the corrupting influence deep inside the Wailing Caverns, underscoring the urgent need to cleanse the Dream's taint."},kw={"ectoplasm","mebok mizzyrix","ratchet","smart drinks","wailing caverns","wailing essence"},rel={"quest:1491","npc:mebok-mizzyrix","zone:wailing","subzone:ratchet","quest:865","zone:barrens"},src={"Wailing Essence","Smart Drinks"}}
E["npc:crane-operator-bigglefuzz"] = {t="npc",n="Crane Operator Bigglefuzz",z="wailing",s="Crane Operator Bigglefuzz is a goblin dockhand working the heavy machinery at the port of Ratchet. After an overloaded crane mishap scattered cargo across the docks, he finds himself desperate to recover a valuable stolen bottle before his superiors notice.",h="Crane Operator Bigglefuzz is a goblin dockhand working the heavy machinery at the port of Ratchet.",sec={{t="Mishap on the Docks",b="Like many goblin dockworkers, Crane Operator Bigglefuzz prioritized efficiency and haste over basic safety margins. While attempting to hoist an excessively heavy haul from a merchant vessel, his crane buckled, sending crates crashing down across the Ratchet wharves. In the ensuing chaos, opportunistic scoundrels swept in, leaving Bigglefuzz to scramble to clean up the mess and salvage the most precious goods before Gazlowe or the local port masters dock his pay.",sp=0},{t="The Stolen Port",b="The worst casualty of the accident was not the broken wood, but a crate containing rare ninety-nine-year-old port. Before Bigglefuzz could secure the spill, an elusive vagrant named Mad Magglish snatched a bottle and fled into hiding, threatening to leave Bigglefuzz answering for an irreplaceable loss.",sp=0}},faq={{q="Who is Crane Operator Bigglefuzz?",a="He is a goblin crane operator stationed along the docks of Ratchet, responsible for loading and unloading sea cargo for the Steamwheedle Cartel.",al={"who is bigglefuzz","crane operator","bigglefuzz ratchet"},it="identity"},{q="What caused the accident at the docks?",a="Bigglefuzz tried to hoist far too much weight at once with his crane, causing the machinery to fail and spilling cargo all over the wharf.",al={"why did the crane drop cargo","ratchet dock accident","crane mishap"},it="history"},{q="Who stole from Bigglefuzz?",a="A shifty troublemaker named Mad Magglish took advantage of the spilled freight to snatch a valuable bottle of ninety-nine-year-old port and slip away.",al={"who took the port","mad magglish cargo","who robbed bigglefuzz"},it="threat"},{q="Why is Bigglefuzz so worried about the stolen bottle?",a="The ninety-nine-year-old port is extraordinarily rare and expensive. Losing it due to negligence means severe financial penalties or worse from the Steamwheedle Cartel bosses.",al={"why does bigglefuzz care about the wine","trouble at the docks reason"},it="why_wanted"},{q="Whose side is Crane Operator Bigglefuzz on?",a="Bigglefuzz works for the Steamwheedle Cartel out of the neutral port of Ratchet. Like most goblins in town, his primary loyalty is to his trade and his employers rather than the Horde or the Alliance, welcoming any adventurer willing to do business or fix a costly mistake.",al={"bigglefuzz faction","who does bigglefuzz work for","crane operator bigglefuzz allegiance"},it="side",add="acbd2274"},{q="What does Crane Operator Bigglefuzz want?",a="Bigglefuzz wants someone to recover the bottle of 99-Year-Old Port that went missing when his cargo spilled all over the docks. A goblin named Mad Magglish made off with the rare vintage, and Bigglefuzz is desperate to get it back before his superiors discover the mishap.",al={"what does bigglefuzz need","bigglefuzz goal","what does bigglefuzz want you to do"},it="wants",add="e72c0e10"},{q="Why is Crane Operator Bigglefuzz here?",a="Bigglefuzz is stationed at the Ratchet docks to operate the heavy loading crane, transferring shipments between merchant vessels and the shore. Unfortunately, an attempt to hoist far too much cargo at once left his crane mangled and the port's freight scattered across the wharf.",al={"why is bigglefuzz in ratchet","bigglefuzz purpose ratchet","why is bigglefuzz at the docks"},it="why_here",add="d46df1e8"},{q="Who is Crane Operator Bigglefuzz tied to?",a="Bigglefuzz is tied to the Steamwheedle Cartel, serving as part of Ratchet's dockside workforce. His current worries tie him directly to the thief Mad Magglish, who swiped valuable liquor from his spilled cargo.",al={"bigglefuzz connections","who is bigglefuzz affiliated with","bigglefuzz cartel"},it="ties",add="eaf0ddf2"}},ang={["profession:Engineering"]="Engineers may appreciate that overloading Steamwheedle rigging and cranes remains the primary cause of industrial accidents along Kalimdor's coastlines.",["class:Rogue"]="Rogues can appreciate how quickly opportunistic thieves like Mad Magglish can exploit a moment of dockside confusion to lift priceless contraband right from under a goblin's nose."},kw={"bigglefuzz","cargo","crane operator","docks","mad magglish","port","ratchet","steamwheedle"},rel={"quest:959","subzone:ratchet","topic:goblin","zone:wailing"},src={"Crane Operator Bigglefuzz"}}
E["npc:ebru"] = {t="npc",n="Ebru",z="wailing",s="Ebru is a night elf druid sheltering in the crags above the Wailing Caverns. As one of Archdruid Naralex's few remaining uncorrupted disciples, she watches helplessly as her master's dream of restoring the Barrens curdles into a nightmare. From her perch, she enlists travelers brave enough to enter the subterranean depths to cull the mutated horrors spawned by the Nightmare.",h="Ebru is a night elf druid sheltering in the crags above the Wailing Caverns.",sec={{t="A Watch Above the Descent",b="While most of Archdruid Naralex's followers succumbed to the emerald corruption creeping through the caverns, Ebru managed to escape the nightmare's grasp. Camped inside the cavernous skull formation overlooking the entrance to the Wailing Caverns, she keeps vigil over the descent. She knows that Naralex's noble plan—to tap subterranean springs and transform the arid Barrens into lush woodland—has gone horribly awry, and she desperately directs willing adventurers to eliminate the burgeoning deviate beasts threatening to overrun the surrounding plains.",sp=0},{t="The Price of Corruption",b="The nightmare twisted not only the ecosystem of the caves, but also Ebru's fellow disciples, turning them into the fanatical Druids of the Fang. Stripped of her companionship and facing the ruin of her circle, Ebru focuses on containment.",sp=1}},faq={{q="Who is Ebru?",a="Ebru is a night elf druid and an uncorrupted disciple of Archdruid Naralex. She resides in a cave high above the entrance to the Wailing Caverns, watching over the site and coordinating efforts to stem the corruption spilling out into the Barrens.",al={"who is ebru","ebru lore","about ebru"},it="identity"},{q="Why is Ebru located above the Wailing Caverns?",a="She fled upward when Naralex's ritual collapsed into the Emerald Nightmare, turning her fellow disciples into hostile zealots. Her perch in the crag above the cave entrance allows her to monitor the caverns while staying safe from the feral horrors inside.",al={"where is ebru","why is ebru up here","ebru cave location"},it="why_here"},{q="What happened to Naralex and his other disciples?",a="Naralex entered a deep trance to tap the underground springs, but his mind became trapped within the Emerald Nightmare. The resulting corruption twisted the cave's flora and fauna and drove most of his disciples mad, transforming them into the Druids of the Fang.",al={"what happened to the disciples","naralex fate","druids of the fang origin"},it="ties"},{q="What does Ebru ask travelers to do?",a="Ebru urges adventurers to delve into the depths of the Wailing Caverns to cull the deviate beasts and strike back against the mutated monstrosities born from her master's tormented dreams.",al={"ebru quests","deviate eradication","cleansing the caverns"},it="wants"},{q="Whose side is Ebru on?",a="Ebru serves the Cenarion Circle and remains loyal to her mentor, the druid Naralex. Unlike many of her peers who fell prey to the nightmare invading the caverns, she has not turned hostile or succumbed to corruption. While she is a night elf, she will welcome any capable traveler—Alliance or Horde alike—willing to venture into the depths to purify the oasis and save her master.",al={"ebru faction","is ebru alliance or horde","who does ebru serve"},it="side",add="5ace5551"}},ang={["class:Druid"]="For druids of the Cenarion Circle, encountering Ebru is a stark reminder of the terrible dangers inherent in walking the Emerald Dream and the catastrophic cost of losing control.",["race:NightElf"]="Ebru represents the small, isolated enclave of night elves operating deep within the arid heart of Kalimdor, far from the ancient boughs of Ashenvale and Teldrassil."},kw={"barrens","cenarion circle","deviate","druid","ebru","naralex","wailing caverns"},rel={"zone:wailing","npc:naralex","quest:1487","zone:barrens","topic:night-elf"},src={"Ebru"}}
E["npc:lady-anacondra"] = {t="npc",n="Lady Anacondra",z="wailing",s="Lady Anacondra is one of the Fanglords leading the Druids of the Fang within the Wailing Caverns. Once a night elf acolyte named Scarletleaf, she was the first to volunteer for Naralex's ambitious effort to heal the Barrens. When her master's Emerald Dream communion turned into a nightmare, her mind broke, twisting her devotion into a venomous drive to see Kalimdor overrun by serpents.",h="Lady Anacondra is one of the Fanglords leading the Druids of the Fang within the Wailing Caverns.",sec={{t="From Scarletleaf to Serpent",b="Before adopting her serpentine title, Lady Anacondra was known as Scarletleaf. When the elder druid Naralex conceived of tapping into the subterranean springs of the Barrens through the Emerald Dream, she stepped forward as his very first volunteer. Her eager loyalty, however, proved her undoing. As Naralex's mind was seized by dark visions, the nightmare seeped out from the dreaming realm and contaminated his disciples, shattering Scarletleaf's sanity and reshaping her reverie into a cold, reptilian obsession.",sp=0},{t="A Fanglord in the Deep",b="Now styling herself Lady Anacondra, she stands guard among the first subterranean chambers of the Wailing Caverns. Like her fellow Fanglords, she abandoned the traditional tenets of the Cenarion Circle in favor of the vicious aspects of the viper. Channeling lightning, nature magic, and slumbering trances, she enforces Naralex's twisted slumber and works to spread the nightmare's corruption into the arid land above.",sp=0}},faq={{q="Who was Lady Anacondra originally?",a="She was originally a young night elf acolyte named Scarletleaf. She was the very first disciple to volunteer to accompany the druid Naralex on his mission into the Barrens.",al={"anacondra real name","who is scarletleaf","scarletleaf backstory"},it="identity"},{q="Why did she turn against the Cenarion Circle?",a="When Naralex attempted to connect to the Emerald Dream beneath the Barrens, his thoughts were overrun by a nightmare. That same nightmare infected the minds of his acolytes, corrupting Scarletleaf and driving her to cast aside her old life to serve the twisted dream.",al={"why is anacondra evil","how did she become a druid of the fang","why did scarletleaf fall"},it="motive"},{q="What is her role in the Wailing Caverns?",a="She serves as one of the four Fanglords leading the Druids of the Fang. She guards the upper reaches of the caverns, ensuring that Naralex remains trapped in his corrupted sleep while dreaming of a reptilian future for the world.",al={"what does anacondra do","lady anacondra purpose","why kill anacondra"},it="purpose"},{q="Where can she be found inside the caverns?",a="Lady Anacondra wanders the first large network of caverns near the entrance of the Wailing Caverns. She patrols among the cavern's raptors and serpents, often shifting between a few resting spots.",al={"anacondra location","where is lady anacondra","anacondra spawn"},it="place",gp=true},{q="What item is taken from her for the Cenarion Circle?",a="She carries the Gem of Anacondra. Slaying her and claiming the gem is required by the druid Nara Wildmane in Thunder Bluff to break the Fanglords' hold over the Barrens.",al={"gem of anacondra","leaders of the fang anacondra","anacondra quest item"},it="item"},{q="What powers does she wield in battle?",a="She draws upon nature magic, striking her foes from afar with searing bolts of lightning and casting magical slumber to incapacitate invaders while her reptilian allies attack.",al={"anacondra abilities","anacondra spells","anacondra attacks"},it="power"},{q="Whose side is Lady Anacondra on?",a="Lady Anacondra stands with the Druids of the Fang, having abandoned her former loyalty to the Cenarion Circle. Corrupted by the Emerald Nightmare that engulfed her master Naralex, she now opposes her former kin and defends the madness festering within the Wailing Caverns.",al={"anacondra faction","who does lady anacondra serve","lady anacondra allegiance"},it="side",add="1a1ef870"},{q="What does Lady Anacondra want?",a="Having discarded her old identity along with her sanity, Lady Anacondra envisions a sinister reptilian future for Azeroth. She seeks to foster the Nightmare's spread and reshape the natural world into a venomous, serpentine domain alongside her fellow Fanglords.",al={"what is anacondra trying to do","anacondra goal","anacondra motivations"},it="wants",add="13dcdd34"},{q="Why is Lady Anacondra here?",a="Originally a young acolyte named Scarletleaf, she was the very first to volunteer when the night elf druid Naralex set out on his mission to restore the arid Barrens. She followed him into the Wailing Caverns to tap the underground springs, only to become trapped and twisted when his dream turned to nightmare.",al={"why is anacondra in wailing caverns","how did anacondra get here","anacondra barrens mission"},it="why_here",add="04976b9c"},{q="Who is Lady Anacondra tied to?",a="Lady Anacondra is tied directly to Naralex, the powerful druid she served as an acolyte before his nightmare broke her mind. She is also bound to the other Fanglords—such as Cobrahn and Serpentis—who rule the twisted cult of the Druids of the Fang alongside her.",al={"who is anacondra master","anacondra naralex connection","who leads anacondra"},it="ties",add="6f9b72fe"}},ang={["class:Druid"]="Anacondra represents a cautionary tragedy for Cenarion druids: an earnest acolyte whose zeal to heal the land made her vulnerable to the nightmare that twisted her communion into madness.",["race:NightElf"]="Seeing a sister of Kaldorei lineage discard her heritage and form in pursuit of a twisted serpentine dream is a sobering reminder of the perils lurking within the Emerald Dream.",["faction:Horde"]="The Horde cannot allow Anacondra and the Fanglords to threaten the delicate lifelines of the Barrens, making her removal critical to securing Crossroads and the nearby oases."},kw={"anacondra","barrens","druids of the fang","fanglord","gem of anacondra","lady anacondra","naralex","scarletleaf","wailing caverns"},rel={"npc:naralex","topic:druids-of-the-fang","quest:914","zone:wailing","zone:barrens","topic:druid"},src={"Lady Anacondra"}}
E["npc:lord-cobrahn"] = {t="npc",n="Lord Cobrahn",z="wailing",s="Lord Cobrahn, formerly the night elf druid Jarlaxla, is one of the corrupted Druids of the Fang lurking deep within the Wailing Caverns. Once renowned within the Cenarion Circle for his mastery of shapeshifting, he succumbed to the nightmare infecting the cavern springs. Renaming himself after his new lethal guise, Cobrahn now commands broods of deviate serpents and defends the twisted labyrinth.",h="Lord Cobrahn, formerly the night elf druid Jarlaxla, is one of the corrupted Druids of the Fang lurking deep...",sec={{t="A Master of Forms Corrupted",b="Before adopting the moniker Lord Cobrahn, Jarlaxla was a respected member of the Cenarion Circle, celebrated among his fellow druids for his extraordinary skill in channeling animal forms. When Naralex ventured into the Wailing Caverns beneath the Barrens hoping to tap their underground springs and restore lush life to the arid wastes, Jarlaxla accompanied him. However, when Naralex's Emerald Dream communion decayed into a twisting nightmare, Jarlaxla's mind shattered alongside his brothers.",sp=0},{t="The Serpent's Embrace",b="Rather than channeling the traditional totemic beasts of Cenarion tradition, the nightmare warped Jarlaxla's shapeshifting prowess into something predatory and reptilian. Adopting the name Lord Cobrahn, he developed a deadly serpentine form that he unleashes in battle. Flanked by venomous deviate pythons and bearing a vicious clawed right hand, he oversees his section of the grottos, violently purging anyone seeking to break the nightmare's hold on the caverns.",sp=0}},faq={{q="Who was Lord Cobrahn before he turned evil?",a="Lord Cobrahn was originally named Jarlaxla. He was a prominent night elf druid within the Cenarion Circle, widely respected for his rare talent and deep affinity for animal shapeshifting forms.",al={"cobrahn real name","who is cobrahn","jarlaxla"},it="origin"},{q="Why is he called Lord Cobrahn?",a="Upon falling victim to the nightmare in the Wailing Caverns, Jarlaxla perfected a lethal serpentine shapeshifting form. He discarded his former name and took the title Lord Cobrahn to reflect his dangerous new power and mastery over serpents.",al={"why cobrahn","lord cobrahn name meaning"},it="name"},{q="Where can Lord Cobrahn be found?",a="Lord Cobrahn resides deep within the Wailing Caverns, a twisting underground network located in the central Barrens, surrounded by deviate pythons and other nightmare-corrupted beasts.",al={"cobrahn location","where is lord cobrahn","cobrahn room"},it="place",gp=true},{q="Why do adventurers need to defeat him?",a="He is one of the primary Fanglords leading the Druids of the Fang. He carries the Gem of Cobrahn, which the druid Nara Wildmane of Thunder Bluff seeks in order to break the Fang leaders' hold over the Barrens.",al={"why kill cobrahn","leaders of the fang cobrahn"},it="purpose"},{q="What unique physical traits does he possess?",a="Unlike ordinary night elves, Cobrahn is noticeably larger in stature, wields a sharp claw on his right hand, and can transform completely into an oversized, venomous snake during combat.",al={"what does cobrahn look like","cobrahn appearance"}},{q="What is his connection to the other Druids of the Fang?",a="Cobrahn is one of the four key Fanglords alongside Lady Anacondra and their kin. They are former Cenarion Circle druids who entered the caverns with Naralex and jointly fell to the twisting corruption of the nightmare.",al={"druids of the fang leaders","cobrahn and anacondra"},it="ties"},{q="Who is Lord Cobrahn?",a="Lord Cobrahn, formerly known as Jarlaxla, is one of the corrupted leaders of the Druids of the Fang lurking deep within the Wailing Caverns. Once a respected night elf druid celebrated within the Cenarion Circle for his mastery of shapeshifting, he fell prey to the dark nightmare that consumed the caverns. Twisted into a monstrous, snake-worshiping hermit, he now wields venomous magic and takes the shape of a massive serpentine beast.",al={"who is cobrahn","lord cobrahn lore","jarlaxla"},it="identity",add="197957cb"},{q="Whose side is Lord Cobrahn on?",a="Lord Cobrahn serves the Druids of the Fang and the spreading nightmare within the Wailing Caverns. He has severed all allegiance to the Cenarion Circle and the night elf people, standing alongside Naralex's fallen disciples against any who dare enter to cleanse the corruption.",al={"cobrahn faction","who does cobrahn serve","lord cobrahn allegiances"},it="side",add="3feb6d50"},{q="Why is Lord Cobrahn here?",a="He originally entered the Wailing Caverns alongside Archdruid Naralex, intending to tap into the subterranean waters and restore the Barrens to a lush paradise. When Naralex's Emerald Dream connection warped into a nightmare, the energies poisoned the minds of his disciples. Cobrahn succumbed completely, remaining in the caverns to guard the slumbering archdruid and foster the nightmare's venomous spawn.",al={"why is cobrahn in wailing caverns","why did cobrahn come here"},it="why_here",add="55d9f433"}},ang={["class:Druid"]="Cobrahn serves as a grim warning of how druidic shapeshifting can be perverted when connected to the nightmare rather than natural balance.",["race:NightElf"]="For night elves, Cobrahn's fall is a bitter tragedy, seeing a skilled brother of the Cenarion Circle abandon his heritage to lead monsters in the subterranean depths.",["faction:Horde"]="Horde adventurers seek Cobrahn to end the foul corruption leaking into the Barrens and protect the fragile ecosystem of Kalimdor's plains."},kw={"cobrahn","deviate python","druids of the fang","fanglord","gem of cobrahn","jarlaxla","lord cobrahn","wailing caverns"},rel={"zone:wailing","quest:914","npc:lady-anacondra","topic:cenarion-circle","topic:druid","topic:night-elf"},src={"Lord Cobrahn"}}
E["npc:lord-pythas"] = {t="npc",n="Lord Pythas",z="wailing",s="Lord Pythas, once a night elf warrior named Aryn, is one of the four corrupted leaders of the Druids of the Fang in the Wailing Caverns. Originally a childhood friend and sworn protector of the archdruid Naralex, he fell victim to the nightmare tainting the oasis underground. Now he wields both martial might and twisted serpent magic against any who try to reach his slumbering master.",h="Lord Pythas, once a night elf warrior named Aryn, is one of the four corrupted leaders of the Druids of the...",sec={{t="A Guardian Falls",b="Before adopting the moniker Pythas, this night elf was known as Aryn. A seasoned warrior and trusted childhood companion to Naralex, he served as the archdruid's personal guard when the expedition ventured into the dry wastes of the Barrens. Eager to better serve Naralex's ambitious dream of restoring lush life to the arid realm, Aryn took up the study of druidism, proving to be an exceptionally fast learner. However, physical discipline and martial valor offered no shelter against the insidious corruption waiting deep within the subterranean fissures.",sp=0},{t="The Lethal Sentinel",b="When Naralex's connection to the Emerald Dream was hijacked by dark nightmares, Aryn's mind succumbed alongside those of his fellow acolytes. Shedding his former name and loyalty, he became Lord Pythas, leader among the Druids of the Fang. Where his fellow serpent lords favor cunning spellcasting or beast forms, Pythas seamlessly blends lethal combat prowess with nature magic. He now prowls the winding tunnels of the caverns, determined to defend the nightmare's twisted grip on the cavern spring.",sp=0}},faq={{q="Who is Lord Pythas?",a="Lord Pythas was originally a night elf warrior named Aryn. He was a childhood friend and personal bodyguard to Archdruid Naralex who studied druidism to assist his master's work in the Barrens.",al={"who is pythas","lord pythas lore","who was aryn"},it="identity"},{q="Why did he turn against Naralex?",a="Pythas did not betray Naralex willingly. When Naralex attempted to tap into the Emerald Dream to heal the Barrens, a nightmare seized the archdruid's thoughts. The corrupting dream seeped into the minds of his acolytes, stripping away Aryn's sanity and remaking him into a serpent lord.",al={"why is pythas evil","how did pythas go mad","why did he become druid of the fang"},it="conflict"},{q="What makes Pythas different from the other Fang leaders?",a="Unlike the other leaders who rely purely on nature magic and beast forms, Pythas was a seasoned warrior before training as a druid. He combines martial combat skill with druidic magic, making him one of the most physically formidable defenders in the caverns.",al={"pythas fighting style","pythas vs other leaders"}},{q="Why do adventurers need to defeat him?",a="Pythas carries one of the four enchanted gems needed to complete the quest Leaders of the Fang. The quest is given by the druid Nara Wildmane in Thunder Bluff, who requires the gems of all four Fang leaders to free the Barrens from their twisted dreams.",al={"leaders of the fang quest","gem of pythas"},it="target"},{q="Where can Lord Pythas be found?",a="Lord Pythas lurks within the deep interior chambers of the Wailing Caverns, surrounded by corrupted beasts and fellow Fang cultists.",al={"pythas location","where is pythas"},it="place",gp=true},{q="What happens to his gem?",a="Upon his defeat, the Gem of Pythas is recovered from his remains. Adventurers bring it, along with the gems of the other three serpent lords, to Nara Wildmane in Thunder Bluff to prove the leadership of the Fang has been broken.",al={"gem of pythas use","what is gem of pythas"},it="item"},{q="Whose side is Lord Pythas on?",a="Lord Pythas serves the Druids of the Fang. Once a devoted protector and acolyte of Naralex, the nightmare took hold of his mind and warped his loyalty. Now, he stands completely aligned with the rogue sect, wielding his blade and nature magic to safeguard the nightmare rather than shield the master he once swore to defend.",al={"pythas faction","pythas alliance","who does pythas serve"},it="side",add="be91010a"},{q="What does Lord Pythas want?",a="Driven mad by the nightmare infecting Naralex's slumber, Pythas seeks to defend the Wailing Caverns from anyone seeking to cleanse them. Stripped of his sanity, he desires only to vanquish intruders who threaten the nightmare's hold, turning his martial discipline and druidic power entirely toward preserving the corrupted domain.",al={"pythas goals","what is pythas trying to do","pythas motive"},it="wants",add="a058df7c"},{q="Why is Lord Pythas in the Wailing Caverns?",a="Pythas originally journeyed into the caverns under his true name, Aryn, serving as Naralex's childhood friend and personal guard during the ritual to restore the Barrens. When Naralex's trance twisted into an inescapable nightmare, Pythas succumbed alongside the other disciples, remaining deep within the caves as a corrupted guardian of the Fang.",al={"why is pythas in wailing caverns","pythas location reason","how did pythas get here"},it="why_here",add="03b88a66"},{q="Who is Lord Pythas tied to?",a="Before his descent into madness, Pythas was known as Aryn, a close childhood friend and personal protector of the archdruid Naralex. He traveled into the underground springs to keep Naralex safe while learning druidism, though the pervasive corruption broke his mind and bound him to the rest of the twisted Leaders of the Fang.",al={"pythas naralex","pythas connections","who does pythas know"},it="ties",add="8f1c0566"},{q="Why is Lord Pythas feared?",a="Lord Pythas is considered the most formidable of the Leaders of the Fang. Unlike many acolytes who rely solely on nature spells, Pythas was a seasoned warrior before taking up druidism. His combination of deadly melee combat prowess, sheer physical resilience, and dark druidic magic makes him exceptionally lethal to any expedition.",al={"is pythas dangerous","why is pythas tough","pythas strength"},it="fame",add="eb0bbb13"}},ang={["class:Druid"]="Pythas represents the tragic fate of a promising acolyte who embraced nature magic out of devotion, only to have the Emerald Dream's corruption twist his teachings into a viperous heresy.",["class:Warrior"]="Before he was corrupted into a serpent cultist, Pythas was a disciplined night elf warrior and personal protector—a grim reminder that martial prowess alone cannot stave off mental madness.",["race:NightElf"]="Watching a respected protector like Aryn fall to dark madness is a bitter sorrow for any night elf seeking to restore balance to the scarred soils of Kalimdor."},kw={"aryn","druids of the fang","gem of pythas","leaders of the fang","lord pythas","naralex","pythas","wailing caverns"},rel={"zone:wailing","npc:naralex","topic:druids-of-the-fang","quest:914","topic:druid","topic:night-elf"},src={"Lord Pythas"}}
E["npc:lord-serpentis"] = {t="npc",n="Lord Serpentis",z="wailing",s="Lord Serpentis is a corrupted night elf druid who stands as one of the four leaders of the rogue Druids of the Fang within the Wailing Caverns. Once a druid of great power and prestige in the order of Naralex, he was twisted into madness when Naralex's dream became a nightmare within the subterranean springs. Now, he helps command the serpent-worshipping sect deep in the caverns where the corrupted Naralex lies slumbering.",h="Lord Serpentis is a corrupted night elf druid who stands as one of the four leaders of the rogue Druids of...",sec={{t="From Noble Druid to Serpent Lord",b="Before darkness overtook the cavern springs, Serpentis was a druid of great power and prestige, one of the noble order led by Naralex that hoped to use the caverns' springs and the Emerald Dream to heal the Barrens. However, when Naralex's vision became a corrupting nightmare, Serpentis was among the druids whose minds fell to the emerging madness.",sp=0},{t="A Lord of the Fang",b="Succumbing completely to the corruption radiating from Naralex's twisted dreams, Serpentis and his fellow druids became the Druids of the Fang. Forsaking traditional Cenarion balance and the totem animals of old, they now seek to remake the Barrens to match their own twisted dreams rather than heal it. Serpentis rules the sect as one of its four leaders, alongside Lady Anacondra, Lord Cobrahn and Lord Pythas.",sp=0},{t="The Final Obstacle",b="Perched deep inside the winding caverns, Lord Serpentis is one of the four leaders of the rogue sect, each of whom carries a dream gem. Those seeking to wake the trapped master or reclaim the waters of the Oasis must strike down Serpentis and claim the gem he carries, breaking the serpent's hold over the labyrinth.",sp=1}},faq={{q="Who is Lord Serpentis?",a="Lord Serpentis is one of the four leaders of the Druids of the Fang, located deep within the Wailing Caverns. Once a night elf druid of great power and prestige in Naralex's order, he was corrupted by Naralex's nightmare along with his fellow druids.",al={"who is serpentis","lord serpentis lore","serpentis background"},it="identity"},{q="Why did Serpentis turn evil?",a="When Naralex's attempt to heal the Barrens through the Emerald Dream turned into a nightmare, its corruption spread to the druids who followed him, turning Serpentis's mind toward madness and serpent worship.",al={"why did serpentis turn","serpentis corruption","why is serpentis bad"},it="motive"},{q="What is his relationship to Naralex?",a="Serpentis was once one of the noble druids who followed Naralex into the caverns. Rather than aiding in his master's recovery, he became a leader of the Druids of the Fang, who now seek to remake the Barrens to match their own twisted dreams.",al={"serpentis and naralex","is serpentis related to naralex","naralex apprentice"},it="ties"},{q="Why do players need to kill him?",a="Serpentis is one of the four leaders of the Druids of the Fang. Eliminating him is essential to break the sect's grip on the Wailing Caverns, secure his gem for the quest Leaders of the Fang, and clear a path toward awakening Naralex.",al={"why kill serpentis","leaders of the fang serpentis","gem of serpentis"},it="target"},{q="Who are the Druids of the Fang?",a="They are a renegade faction of night elf druids who followed Naralex into the Wailing Caverns. Corrupted by the Emerald Nightmare, they abandoned traditional druidic forms to adopt the aspects, venoms, and behaviors of serpents under the command of Serpentis and their other fanglords.",al={"druids of the fang lore","what are druids of the fang","fang druids"},it="people"},{q="Whose side is Lord Serpentis on?",a="Lord Serpentis is the leader of the Druids of the Fang. Corrupted by the nightmare consuming his mentor Naralex, he has abandoned the Cenarion Circle and the ideals of the night elves, turning entirely hostile to all who enter the caverns.",al={"lord serpentis faction","who does serpentis serve","serpentis allegiance"},it="side",add="1f07cf4d"},{q="What does Lord Serpentis want?",a="Originally driven by a deep ambition to become a shan'do—an honored teacher like his mentor Naralex—his desires were warped into madness by the Emerald Nightmare. Now insane, he seeks to hold dominion over the caverns with his twisted followers, proclaiming himself the supreme master of the serpents.",al={"serpentis goal","what does serpentis want","serpentis motives"},it="wants",add="961c3dfc"},{q="Why is Lord Serpentis in the Wailing Caverns?",a="Serpentis originally came to the Wailing Caverns as Naralex's finest student, helping his mentor tap into the subterranean springs to restore the Barrens. When Naralex lost control of his dream and nightmare corruptions erupted, Serpentis fell victim to the psychic torment and remained inside to claim the caves as ruler of the Druids of the Fang.",al={"why is serpentis here","why is lord serpentis in wailing caverns","lord serpentis location reason"},it="why_here",add="54e444da"}},ang={["class:Druid"]="Serpentis represents the tragic danger lurking within the Emerald Dream, showcasing how even a druid of great power can be twisted when a noble vision becomes a nightmare.",["race:NightElf"]="For night elves, Serpentis and his followers are a painful disgrace—kaldorei scholars of great renown who threw away their sacred duty to nature to become monstrous serpent lords.",["race:Tauren"]="Tauren see the corruption of Serpentis as a foul desecration of the Earth Mother's balance, threatening the fragile ecosystem of the Barrens with unnatural madness."},kw={"druids of the fang","gem of serpentis","leaders of the fang","lord serpentis","naralex","serpentis","wailing caverns"},rel={"npc:naralex","zone:wailing","quest:914","topic:druids-of-the-fang","topic:druid","topic:night-elf"},src={"Lord Serpentis"}}
E["npc:mutanus-the-devourer"] = {t="npc",n="Mutanus the Devourer",z="wailing",s="Mutanus the Devourer is a monstrous, pale murloc manifested directly from the Emerald Nightmare. Lurking in the darkest recesses of the sleeping druid Naralex's mind, it emerges to devour anyone attempting to break the Nightmare's hold over the Wailing Caverns. Slaying this twisted aberration is the final step in freeing Naralex from his tormented slumber.",h="Mutanus the Devourer is a monstrous, pale murloc manifested directly from the Emerald Nightmare.",sec={{t="A Dreamer's Worst Fear",b="When the night elf druid Naralex tapped into the underground springs beneath the Barrens, he aimed to restore life to the arid wastes by connecting them to the Emerald Dream. Instead, an ancient corruption known as the Emerald Nightmare invaded his thoughts. Trapped in an agonizing vision, Naralex's subconscious fears took physical form. The corruption seized upon a bizarre, primal revulsion in the druid's psyche—his deep-seated terror of murlocs—and amplified it into an immense, albino predator.",sp=0},{t="The Waking Nightmare",b="Mutanus was sent forth into the waking world by the dark force infesting Naralex's mind, tasked with ensuring the druid never awakens. When a Disciple of Naralex performs the ritual to revive their master, Mutanus breaches the boundary between dream and reality. Along with his unnatural form, he brings alien relics from the dreamscape, such as the mysterious Deep Fathom Ring. Until Mutanus falls, Naralex remains a prisoner of his own corrupted imagination.",sp=1}},faq={{q="What is Mutanus the Devourer?",a="Mutanus the Devourer is an enormous, pale murloc-like aberration born from the Emerald Nightmare. He is not a normal denizen of Azeroth, but a living nightmare summoned into reality from the corrupted mind of the sleeping druid Naralex.",al={"who is mutanus","what kind of creature is mutanus","is mutanus a murloc"},it="identity"},{q="Why does Mutanus look like a giant murloc?",a="The Nightmare twisted Naralex's subconscious thoughts and drew out his worst personal enemy: murlocs. The corruption weaponized that deep-seated fear, manifesting it as a colossal albino monstrosity.",al={"why murloc","why is mutanus a murloc","naralex murloc fear"},it="origin"},{q="Why does Mutanus appear at the end of the ritual?",a="The dark presence corrupting the Emerald Dream ordered Mutanus to prevent anyone from breaking Naralex's slumber. When Naralex's disciples begin the awakening ritual, Mutanus crosses over into the physical cavern to devour the rescuers.",al={"when does mutanus spawn","why summon mutanus","naralex ritual boss"},it="why_here"},{q="Where does Mutanus come from?",a="Mutanus originates from the Emerald Nightmare, the corrupted realm that has ensnared Naralex. Crossing over from the dreamscape into Azeroth, he even brought along strange relics like the Deep Fathom Ring.",al={"mutanus origin","is mutanus from the nightmare","emerald nightmare mutanus"},it="origin"},{q="Does killing Mutanus save Naralex?",a="Yes. Once Mutanus is slain, the nightmare's immediate hold over Naralex's mind is shattered, allowing his disciples to successfully awaken the druid and break the cavern's dark trance.",al={"is naralex saved","what happens after mutanus dies","waking naralex"},sp=1,it="next_step"},{q="Why is Mutanus immune to shadow magic?",a="Mutanus is an aberration woven from dark nightmare energies, making him naturally resilient against necrotic and shadow spells that would harm mundane beasts.",al={"mutanus shadow immunity","shadow spells mutanus","is mutanus shadow immune"},it="power"},{q="Whose side is Mutanus the Devourer on?",a="Mutanus serves whatever dark, corrupting force has infected the Emerald Dream and trapped Naralex in his nightmare. Rather than acting on his own whims or serving the native wildlife of the Barrens, he obeys the will of the Nightmare itself, sent forth into the waking world solely to ensure the druid remains asleep and corrupted.",al={"who controls mutanus","mutanus faction","mutanus allegiance"},it="side",add="1d17d2ec"},{q="What does Mutanus the Devourer want?",a="Mutanus exists to disrupt any attempt to wake Naralex from his twisted slumber. He seeks to devour anyone who tries to liberate the sleeping druid from the Nightmare's grip, ensuring Naralex remains helpless while the dark corruption continues to fester within the Wailing Caverns.",al={"mutanus goal","why does mutanus fight","what is mutanus trying to do"},it="wants",add="93f250d8"},{q="Who is Mutanus the Devourer tied to?",a="Mutanus is directly tied to the night elf druid Naralex. He is not a natural beast born of the Barrens, but a physical manifestation born from the darkest corners of Naralex's own corrupted mind, embodying the druid's subconscious fears as a twisted nightmare in the physical world.",al={"mutanus connection naralex","mutanus relationship naralex","who is mutanus linked to"},it="ties",add="c0fe9c52"}},ang={["class:Druid"]="Mutanus represents the terrifying hazards of delving too deeply into the Emerald Dream without safeguards, as a fellow druid's mind was completely overtaken by corruption.",["race:NightElf"]="For the kaldorei, Mutanus is a tragedy brought to life, embodying how Naralex's noble ambitions to heal the Barrens warped into a monstrous nightmare.",["faction:Horde"]="The Horde cannot allow Mutanus and the Nightmare to corrupt the heart of the Barrens, threatening the vital oasis waters needed to sustain Durotar and Mulgore."},kw={"albino murloc","barrens","deep fathom ring","devourer","emerald nightmare","murloc","mutanus","naralex","wailing caverns"},rel={"npc:naralex","zone:wailing","topic:emerald-dream","topic:murloc","topic:druid"},src={"Mutanus the Devourer"}}
E["npc:nalpak"] = {t="npc",n="Nalpak",z="wailing",s="Nalpak is a tauren druid disciple who watches over the troubled Wailing Caverns in the Barrens. Stationed in the high cliff-cave overlooking the cavern entrance, he enlists passing adventurers to help contain the nightmare twisting the subterranean ecosystem.",h="Nalpak is a tauren druid disciple who watches over the troubled Wailing Caverns in the Barrens.",sec={{t="Watcher Above the Caverns",b="Perched inside a hidden cavern directly above the mouth of the Wailing Caverns, Nalpak remains loyal to the vision of Archdruid Naralex. While his master lies trapped in a corrupted slumber deep below, Nalpak works to keep the spreading corruption at bay. He asks adventurers to gather deviate hides for use as leather.",sp=0}},faq={{q="Where is Nalpak located?",a="Nalpak is located in a cave high up on the rock face directly above the natural rock formation that leads into the Wailing Caverns in the central Barrens.",al={"nalpak location","where is nalpak","find nalpak"},it="place",gp=true},{q="Who is Nalpak?",a="He is a tauren druid and one of the Disciples of Naralex, tasked with monitoring the emergence of twisted creatures from the Wailing Caverns while his master attempts to restore the Barrens through the Emerald Dream.",al={"who is nalpak","nalpak lore"},it="identity"},{q="Why does Nalpak want deviate hides?",a="Nalpak wants to examine the hides of the deviate creatures infesting the Wailing Caverns. Despite their evil nature, he believes their unusual hides can be put to good use in leatherworking.",al={"why deviate hides","deviate hides quest"},it="wants"},{q="What is Nalpak's relationship to Naralex?",a="Nalpak is a faithful student and follower of Archdruid Naralex, serving as one of the disciples sent to support the ambitious attempt to reawaken the springs of the Barrens.",al={"is nalpak naralex disciple","nalpak and naralex"},it="ties"},{q="Whose side is Nalpak on?",a="Nalpak is a disciple of Naralex and acts in service to the druids seeking to heal the Barrens. While he is a tauren welcoming to those who enter the caverns to aid their cause, his foremost allegiance lies with Naralex's vision and the restoration of the corrupted subterranean springs.",al={"nalpak faction","who does nalpak serve","is nalpak horde"},it="side",add="a6c930b7"},{q="Why is Nalpak at the Wailing Caverns?",a="Nalpak came to the Wailing Caverns alongside Archdruid Naralex and fellow disciples to channel the Emerald Dream into the arid Barrens. After the ritual went terribly awry, he remained posted near the cavern entrance to enlist adventurers in gathering corrupted materials and dealing with the twisted beasts inside.",al={"why is nalpak here","nalpak wailing caverns reason","what brought nalpak here"},it="why_here",add="668cdd3e"}},ang={["class:Druid"]="For fellow druids, Nalpak is a grim reminder of how perilous touching the Emerald Dream can be when darkness takes root in what was meant to be a restorative ritual.",["race:Tauren"]="Nalpak represents the tauren dedication to healing the parched lands of Kalimdor, refusing to abandon the mission even when disaster strikes the dreamers."},kw={"barrens druid","deviate hides","disciples of naralex","nalpak","naralex","tauren","wailing caverns"},rel={"npc:naralex","zone:wailing","quest:1486","zone:barrens","topic:tauren"},src={"Nalpak"}}
E["npc:naralex"] = {t="npc",n="Naralex",z="wailing",s="Naralex is a night elf druid who sought to restore the parched Barrens to a lush forest using the powers of the Emerald Dream. Instead, his slumber was overtaken by a dark nightmare, twisting the Wailing Caverns beneath the earth and turning his followers into venomous fiends.",h="Naralex is a night elf druid who sought to restore the parched Barrens to a lush forest using the powers of...",sec={{t="A Vision of Green",b="Long before the Great Sundering, the sun-scorched plains of the Barrens were once a vibrant forest. Viewing this loss as a tragedy, Naralex journeyed south from Darnassus with a cohort of devoted disciples to reverse the drought. Deep beneath the savannah, he discovered an intricate subterranean network of underground springs and rushing geysers, naming them the Wailing Caverns after the howling wind and steam that moaned through the rock. He believed that by entering a deep trance and channeling the pristine energies of the Emerald Dream into these subterranean waters, the life-giving flow would reach the surface and cause the entire wasteland to bloom.",sp=0},{t="The Waking Nightmare",b="Naralex seated himself in deep meditation deep within the subterranean caverns, but his noble design collapsed the moment his consciousness touched the realm of the Dream. Rather than finding peaceful fonts of wild nature, his mind was ensnared by a malignant, encroaching corruption—an Emerald Nightmare. The festering corruption seized the sleeping druid's body, transforming him into an open conduit through which dark energies bled into the living world. The pristine springs turned foul, sprouting mutated fungal blooms and warping the native beasts of the caverns into ravenous deviate horrors.",sp=0},{t="Fallen Disciples",b="The nightmare did not stop with the wildlife. Naralex's own disciples, driven completely mad by the psychic backlash bleeding out of their master's trance, broke away from the traditions of the Cenarion Circle. Casting aside their reverence for balance, they took on serpent forms and renamed themselves the Druids of the Fang. Believing their twisted growth must spread across Kalimdor, they now guard Naralex's slumbering body to ensure he never wakes, leaving only a few loyal disciples, such as Muyoh, searching for allies brave enough to break the trance.",sp=1}},faq={{q="Who is Naralex?",a="Naralex is a night elf druid of the Cenarion Circle. He led an expedition into the Wailing Caverns with the goal of tapping into the Emerald Dream to turn the arid Barrens back into the lush forest it had been before the Sundering.",al={"naralex lore","who is the sleeping elf","wailing caverns sleeper"},it="identity"},{q="Why is Naralex asleep inside the Wailing Caverns?",a="He entered a meditative trance to channel energies directly from the Emerald Dream into the underground aquifers beneath the Barrens. However, an overwhelming nightmare seized his mind, trapping him in a fevered slumber that he cannot wake from on his own.",al={"why is naralex sleeping","what is naralex doing","naralex trance"},it="why_here"},{q="What created the Druids of the Fang?",a="They were originally Naralex's faithful disciples. When the Emerald Nightmare corrupted Naralex's dream connection, the leaking malice drove his followers insane. They abandoned the Cenarion Circle, embraced serpent totems, and now protect his slumber to keep the corruption spreading.",al={"druids of the fang origin","who are druids of the fang","naralex disciples"},it="threat"},{q="What caused the Wailing Caverns to mutate?",a="Naralex's sleeping body became an open conduit for the Emerald Nightmare. The foul dream energies seeped directly into the subterranean river system, warping the caverns' plants, crocodiles, raptors, and serpents into aggressive deviate mutants.",al={"why is wailing caverns corrupted","deviate beasts origin","wailing caverns fungus"},it="history"},{q="Can Naralex be awakened?",a="Yes, with outside help. His remaining loyal disciple, Muyoh, works with adventurers willing to enter the depths, slay the twisted Druids of the Fang, and perform a ritual to break the grip of the nightmare on Naralex's mind.",al={"how to save naralex","waking naralex","naralex quest"},sp=1,it="next_step"},{q="Why did Naralex want to change the Barrens?",a="Naralex learned that the Barrens was once a flourishing forest before the Great Sundering shattered Kalimdor. He saw its current arid condition as an ecological wound and wished to restore its ancient verdant canopy.",al={"why regrow the barrens","naralex barrens goal","why the barrens"},it="wants"},{q="Whose side is Naralex on?",a="Naralex belongs to the Cenarion Circle, making him neutral toward both the Alliance and the Horde. His loyalties lie with the balance of nature rather than the political squabbles of Kalimdor. Unfortunately, his trapped mind has lost control entirely, leaving his slumbering body guarded by twisted former acolytes who attack anyone that enters.",al={"is naralex alliance or horde","naralex faction","who does naralex serve"},it="side",add="ec55d9d1"},{q="Who is Naralex tied to?",a="Naralex is a venerable night elf druid of the Cenarion Circle who brought a retinue of faithful disciples to the Barrens. Most of his followers succumbed to the dark nightmare gripping his mind and transformed into the monstrous Druids of the Fang. Only a lone disciple, the tauren Muyoh, remains uncorrupted and watches anxiously outside.",al={"naralex allies","naralex disciples","who are naralex's followers"},it="ties",add="705828d6"}},ang={["class:Druid"]="Naralex serves as a grim cautionary tale to druids: meddling blindly with primal natural states or tapping too deeply into the Dream without caution can unleash catastrophic perversions of the wild.",["race:NightElf"]="While Naralex sought to heal Kalimdor, his unchecked ambition deep in Horde territory brought disgrace to the Cenarion Circle and spawned the treacherous Druids of the Fang.",["race:Tauren"]="The twisted waters beneath the Barrens pose an immediate threat to the oasis pools and wildlife that sustain the tribes of Mulgore and the savannah.",["faction:Horde"]="A night elf's failed mystical experiment has polluted the heart of the Barrens, forcing Horde forces from the Crossroads to deal with the rampaging beasts boiling up from the cavern."},kw={"cenarion circle","deviate","druids of the fang","emerald dream","emerald nightmare","muyoh","naralex","the barrens","wailing caverns"},rel={"zone:wailing","topic:druids-of-the-fang","topic:emerald-dream","topic:cenarion-circle","topic:druid","zone:barrens","topic:night-elf","quest:1489"},src={"Naralex"}}
E["npc:verdan-the-everliving"] = {t="npc",n="Verdan the Everliving",z="wailing",s="Verdan the Everliving is a colossal bog beast lurking deep within the verdant tunnels of the Wailing Caverns. Once a peaceful protector of the underground springs and flora, he was twisted by the waking nightmare radiating from the sleeping druid Naralex. Now bound to the corrupted Druids of the Fang, Verdan violently attacks any who venture into his damp hollows.",h="Verdan the Everliving is a colossal bog beast lurking deep within the verdant tunnels of the Wailing Caverns.",sec={{t="Guardian of the Lush Depths",b="Long before Naralex arrived to tap into the natural springs of the Barrens, Verdan was formed from the overgrown foliage, silt, and moisture filling the caves. Thought to be the original guardian spirit of the subterranean oasis, Verdan was an ancient, gentle elemental keeping watch over the underground flora.",sp=0},{t="Twisted by the Nightmare",b="When Naralex attempted to cultivate the dry Barrens into a lush paradise, his ritual fractured into a vivid nightmare within the Emerald Dream. The resulting corruption bled through the subterranean waters, tainting everything living inside the cavern. Verdan could not resist the pervasive blight; his gentle temperament vanished, leaving behind an enormous, hostile brute sworn to protect the mad Druids of the Fang.",sp=1}},faq={{q="What kind of creature is Verdan?",a="Verdan is a massive bog beast, an elemental being animated out of plant matter, peat, and subterranean mire. He formed naturally from the rich flora of the caves long ago.",al={"verdan monster type","what is verdan","verdan race"},it="origin"},{q="Why is Verdan hostile to adventurers?",a="Verdan was once a peaceful guardian of the caverns, but the nightmare emanating from the slumbering Archdruid Naralex corrupted his mind. Now maddened, he perceives all outside intruders as trespassers to be crushed.",al={"why does verdan attack","verdan hostile","is verdan evil"},it="hostile"},{q="What is Verdan's connection to the Druids of the Fang?",a="Both Verdan and the Druids of the Fang fell victim to the same corrupting nightmare. Sharing this twisted vision, Verdan acts as an ally and enforcer for the insane druids, guarding the deeper reaches of the caverns.",al={"verdan druids of the fang","verdan fang connection"},it="ties"},{q="Where in the Wailing Caverns is Verdan located?",a="Verdan dwells in a cavernous, mossy chamber deep in the winding paths of the Wailing Caverns, past several of the corrupted Fang leaders.",al={"where is verdan","verdan location","how to find verdan"},it="place",gp=true},{q="Can Verdan be cured or cleansed?",a="There is no known way to cleanse Verdan. The nightmare took deep root in his elemental form, leaving adventurers no choice but to destroy the hulking beast to ensure safe passage through the cavern.",al={"can verdan be saved","save verdan","purify verdan"}},{q="Why was Verdan called 'the Everliving'?",a="The origin of his epithet is unknown. Verdan is an ancient bog beast formed from the Wailing Caverns' lush foliage.",al={"why everliving","everliving meaning","verdan name origin"},it="name"},{q="Who is Verdan the Everliving?",a="Verdan the Everliving is a colossal plant elemental, formed long ago from the flourishing flora within the Wailing Caverns. Once a peaceful protector of the underground ecosystem, he was twisted and corrupted when Naralex's Emerald Dream connection soured into a nightmare. Now transformed into a towering abomination, he fiercely attacks any living creature that crosses his path.",al={"who is verdan","verdan the everliving","what is verdan"},it="identity",add="01116030"},{q="Whose side is Verdan the Everliving on?",a="Verdan is allied with the corrupted Druids of the Fang. When the Nightmare claimed the caverns and drove the druids mad, it ensnared the ancient guardian as well. He now defends the depths in unison with the cultists against any outsiders seeking to disturb them or wake Naralex.",al={"verdan faction","is verdan with the druids","verdan allegiances"},it="side",add="19c7064f"},{q="What does Verdan the Everliving want?",a="Stripped of his gentle demeanor by the Nightmare, Verdan has no grand scheme beyond territorial defense and destruction. Driven by corrupted instincts, he maintains a relentless vigil over the deep caverns, seeking only to crush any trespassers who venture near his lair.",al={"verdan goal","what does verdan want","verdan motive"},it="wants",add="67c0a7ba"},{q="Why is Verdan the Everliving here?",a="Verdan originated within the Wailing Caverns itself, coalescing ages ago from the lush, subterranean vegetation fed by the underground springs. He has always served as the original guardian of these caves and remains bound to the realm where he grew.",al={"why is verdan in wailing caverns","how did verdan get here","verdan origin here"},it="why_here",add="238e0c9d"},{q="Why is Verdan the Everliving feared?",a="Verdan is feared as the most physically brutal monster within the Wailing Caverns. His immense size and plant-hewn strength allow him to deliver devastating blows capable of crushing an armored warrior in mere seconds.",al={"why is verdan feared","is verdan dangerous","how strong is verdan"},it="fame",add="357d8159"}},ang={["class:Druid"]="Verdan's fall is a tragic reminder of what happens when natural elemental wardens are poisoned by a corrupted Emerald Dream.",["class:Shaman"]="As an elemental spirit of earth and water grown warped and violent, putting down Verdan is an act of restoring balance to the fractured elements of the Barrens.",["faction:Horde"]="Because the Wailing Caverns sit at the heart of the Barrens, defeating dangerous beasts like Verdan is essential to protecting nearby crossroads and settlements."},kw={"bog beast","druids of the fang","elemental","everliving","naralex","nightmare","verdan","wailing caverns"},rel={"zone:wailing","npc:naralex","quest:1012","topic:druid"},src={"Verdan the Everliving"}}
E["quest:1486"] = {t="quest",n="Deviate Hides",z="wailing",s="Deviate Hides is a task given by Nalpak, a disciple of Naralex stationed above the entrance to the Wailing Caverns. While Naralex lies trapped in a twisted nightmare, Nalpak seeks to salvage something useful from the mutated beasts spawned beneath the Barrens. By gathering skins from these deviate predators, he hopes to put their strange, otherworldly properties to practical use.",h="Deviate Hides is a task given by Nalpak, a disciple of Naralex stationed above the entrance to the Wailing...",sec={{t="Corruption Made Manifest",b="When the night elf druid Naralex attempted to tap the subterranean springs beneath the Barrens to restore lush life to the arid plains, his mind slipped into a terrifying nightmare. That dark reverie bled into reality, mutating the native wildlife of the Wailing Caverns into vicious deviate beasts. Raptors, crocolisks, vipers, and shambling horrors emerged warped and aggressive, altered by the emerald corruption leaking from their dreaming master.",sp=0},{t="A Pragmatic Druid",b="Perched in the rock formation above the cavern mouth, Nalpak watches the disaster unfold with a mix of dread and practical curiosity. Though he recognizes the deviate creatures as inherently malignant and unnatural, he believes their corrupted forms might yield unique materials. In particular, their toughened, warped pelts possess resilience that could benefit skilled leatherworkers, turning the fruits of a tragic nightmare into durable equipment.",sp=0}},faq={{q="Where can I find Nalpak?",a="Nalpak and his fellow disciples have established a small camp high up in the rock formation resembling a skull above the Wailing Caverns entrance. Rather than walking straight into the main tunnel, climb the mountain slopes behind the cave mouth and carefully drop down into the upper cavern eye-socket ledge overlooking the oasis.",al={"nalpak location","where is nalpak","how to find nalpak","quest giver deviate hides"},it="place",gp=true},{q="What are deviate creatures?",a="Deviate creatures are local beasts transformed by the Emerald Nightmare that escaped from Naralex's slumbering mind. Raptors, snakes, crocolisks, and wind serpents native to the Barrens have been twisted into darker, vicious forms with strange magical properties and mottled, unnatural hides.",al={"what are deviates","deviate beasts","why are animals mutated in wailing caverns"},it="target"},{q="Why does Nalpak want these hides?",a="Nalpak recognizes that while the beasts are born of evil corruption, their hides exhibit unusual, otherworldly strength. He believes that by studying and working the pelts, leatherworkers can repurpose the nightmare's taint into resilient gear.",al={"why deviate hides","what does nalpak want hides for","purpose of deviate hides"},it="motive"},{q="Can any deviate creature drop the hides?",a="The mutated beasts prowling throughout the tunnels and interior of the Wailing Caverns carry these skins. Hunters and leatherworkers often find skinning the beasts yields extra pelts beyond what can simply be scavenged from their remains.",al={"which mobs drop deviate hides","who drops deviate hide","deviate hide farm"},it="item",gp=true},{q="Is Nalpak aligned with the Horde or the Alliance?",a="Nalpak is a disciple of Naralex and belongs to the Cenarion Circle. He remains neutral and will accept aid from any capable adventurer, whether Alliance or Horde, who is brave enough to enter the corrupted caves.",al={"is nalpak horde","is deviate hides alliance","can alliance do deviate hides"},it="side"},{q="What happened to Naralex?",a="Naralex sought to awaken the underground springs of the Barrens by connecting his consciousness to the Emerald Dream. Instead, his slumber was seized by the Nightmare, transforming the cavern system into a breeding ground for horrors and leaving him comatose deep within the caves.",al={"who is naralex","naralex nightmare","what happened to the druid in wailing caverns"},it="history"},{q="What is the Deviate Hide for?",a="Deviate hides possess strange, otherworldly properties born from the nightmare corrupting the caverns. While the creatures they come from are twisted and hostile, Nalpak believes their unusual pelts can be repurposed through leatherworking to craft sturdy armor and packs, bringing something useful out of the corruption.",al={"deviate hide use","why gather deviate hides","deviate hide purpose"},it="item",add="58e10be2"}},ang={["class:Druid"]="Nalpak's camp represents the Cenarion Circle's grim vigil over an initiative gone terribly wrong, making the task of containing the cavern's mutations personal for fellow druids.",["profession:Herbalism"]="The abnormal growth feeding the deviate beasts is directly tied to the corrupted flora and underground springs winding through the cavern network."},kw={"barrens","cenarion circle","deviate","deviate hides","emerald nightmare","leatherworking","nalpak","naralex","wailing caverns"},rel={"npc:nalpak","zone:wailing","npc:naralex","zone:barrens"},m={start="Nalpak",level="17",faction="Neutral",id=1486,ri={"Deviate Hide"}},src={"Deviate Hides (Classic)"}}
E["quest:1487"] = {t="quest",n="Deviate Eradication",z="wailing",s="Deviate Eradication is a task assigned by the night elf druid Ebru above the entrance to the Wailing Caverns. While other disciples focus on waking their slumbering leader, Ebru asks adventurers to purge the caverns of mutated deviate beasts spawned by his twisted vision. Ridding the subterranean oasis of these horrors is an essential step in stemming the corruption threatening the Barrens.",h="Deviate Eradication is a task assigned by the night elf druid Ebru above the entrance to the Wailing Caverns.",sec={{t="A Dream Gone Terribly Wrong",b="The night elf druid Naralex brought his followers to the subterranean springs of the Barrens with an ambitious vision: tap into the Emerald Dream to regrow the parched plains into a lush, thriving woodland. Instead, Naralex became ensnared within the Dream, his slumber twisting into an agonizing nightmare. Rather than healing the land, the power surging through the caverns warped the native wildlife and plant life into monstrous, aggressive mutants known as deviate beasts.",sp=0},{t="Ebru's Stand",b="Perched in the cliff-face cavern overlooking the cave entrance, Ebru and a handful of surviving Disciples of Naralex watch in despair as their numbers dwindle. While some among them dedicate their energy toward awakening their fallen master, Ebru recognizes an immediate crisis. Left unchecked, the rapidly multiplying deviate vipers, shamblers, ravagers, and dreadfangs will spill outward into the Barrens. Ebru therefore recruits passing adventurers to descend into the deep tunnels and cull the aberrant monstrosities at their source.",sp=0}},faq={{q="Where do I find Ebru to start this quest?",a="Ebru is stationed with a few fellow Disciples of Naralex in a secluded cave perched high above the main mouth of the Wailing Caverns, resting inside what resembles the right eye socket of the skull-shaped rock formation. Reaching her typically requires climbing around the mountain ridge and carefully dropping down onto the upper ledge.",al={"ebru location","where is ebru","how to get to ebru","wailing caverns eye cave"},it="place",gp=true},{q="What caused the beasts to become deviate?",a="The creatures were mutated by dark energies seeping from the Emerald Dream. When the druid Naralex linked his consciousness to the subterranean springs to rejuvenate the Barrens, his mind was hijacked by a nightmare, warping the restorative energies into a corrupting force that mutates local wildlife into deviate monsters.",al={"why are they deviate","deviate beasts origin","what corrupted the animals in wc"},it="origin"},{q="Who are the Disciples of Naralex?",a="The Disciples of Naralex are a circle of druidic followers who accompanied Naralex to the Wailing Caverns to help revitalize the Barrens. Following his entrapment within the Nightmare, many turned feral or fell into madness, leaving only a tiny remnant of sane disciples trying to undo the disaster.",al={"disciples of naralex","naralex followers","who are the druids in wailing caverns"},it="people"},{q="Can Alliance and Horde both take this quest?",a="Yes. Ebru and her companions are neutral druids concerned with the preservation of nature and the containment of the Nightmare. They accept assistance from capable champions of either the Horde or the Alliance.",al={"deviate eradication alliance or horde","is deviate eradication neutral"},it="side",gp=true},{q="What creatures do you have to slay for Ebru?",a="Ebru directs you to hunt down four specific breeds of corrupted fauna deep within the caverns: Deviate Ravagers, Deviate Vipers, Deviate Shamblers, and Deviate Dreadfangs, slaying seven of each.",al={"deviate eradication mobs","deviate eradication targets","which deviate to kill"},it="target",gp=true},{q="Does completing this quest wake Naralex?",a="No. Ebru's assignment focuses strictly on pest control and damage mitigation by thinning out the dangerous beasts. Awakening Naralex requires a direct ritual performed deep inside his sanctum at the heart of the cavern.",al={"does this wake naralex","how to wake naralex"},it="next_step",gp=true},{q="Why does Ebru want the deviate beasts destroyed?",a="While other Disciples of Naralex focus their efforts on awakening their trapped master, Ebru sees an immediate threat festering within the Wailing Caverns. Naralex's vision of restoring the Barrens back into a lush forest has devolved into a nightmare, spewing corrupt, unnatural creatures throughout the tunnels. Ebru believes there is no hope of healing these lands or saving their leader until these twisted beasts are purged from the caverns.",al={"ebru motive","why kill deviate beasts","why does ebru want deviate beasts dead"},it="motive",add="62e049f1"},{q="What are the deviate creatures in the Wailing Caverns?",a="They are the local fauna—vipers, raptors, and shambling plant horrors—warped into monstrous forms by the dark energies leaking from Naralex's nightmare. Naralex sought to channel the Emerald Dream to revitalize the arid Barrens, but when his dream turned foul, the ambient magical spillway mutated the wildlife into aggressive, unnatural predators that now infest the cavern depths.",al={"what are deviate ravagers","deviate beasts wailing caverns","corrupt creatures wailing caverns"},it="target",add="b4bfe70b"},{q="Why can't the Disciples of Naralex clear the caverns themselves?",a="The disciples are stretched far too thin to mount an assault on their own. Their order has dwindled significantly since Naralex became ensnared in his nightmare, and those few who remain are divided between preparing a ritual to awaken him and defending what little foothold they still maintain. They lack the numbers and martial strength to push into the caves and exterminate the beasts without outside assistance.",al={"why does ebru need my help","why cant disciples clear caves","disciples of naralex why need help"},it="why_me",add="ab17f40e"}},ang={["class:Druid"]="The twisted ecosystem within the caverns serves as a somber warning of what happens when communion with the Emerald Dream turns disastrous.",["faction:Horde"]="Because the Wailing Caverns sit in the very heart of Kalimdor's central plains, culling these aggressive predators is vital to protecting nearby settlements like the Crossroads.",["race:NightElf"]="Witnessing Naralex's noble aspiration collapse into nightmare-born horror is a heavy burden for kaldorei travelers, who feel a duty to assist their stranded kin."},kw={"barrens","deviate dreadfang","deviate eradication","deviate ravager","deviate shambler","deviate viper","ebru","naralex","wailing caverns"},rel={"npc:ebru","npc:naralex","zone:wailing","zone:barrens","topic:emerald-dream"},m={start="Ebru",level="21",faction="Neutral",id=1487},src={"Deviate Eradication"}}
E["quest:1489"] = {t="quest",n="Hamuul Runetotem",z="wailing",s="This quest directs Horde adventurers from the lush but troubled oases of the Barrens to the lofty heights of Thunder Bluff. Tonga Runetotem suspects a deep spiritual corruption within the Wailing Caverns and sends you to seek the guidance of Archdruid Hamuul Runetotem.",h="This quest directs Horde adventurers from the lush but troubled oases of the Barrens to the lofty heights of...",sec={{t="A Disturbing Dream",b="While studying the wildlife of the Barrens, Tonga Runetotem identified a strange affliction gripping the creatures near the lush oases. The altered beasts carried shells tainted by an unnatural force, leading Tonga to realize that the land itself is trapped in a delirious, troubled dream. Convinced that the waters flowing from the subterranean Wailing Caverns are the origin of this rot, Tonga knows that venturing inside requires far greater wisdom than a lone naturalist possesses.",sp=0},{t="Counsel on Elder Rise",b="To understand the threat within the caverns, Tonga directs you to Thunder Bluff to confer with his kin, Archdruid Hamuul Runetotem. Hamuul is the highest-ranking tauren druid and a revered spiritual leader of the Cenarion Circle in Mulgore. Stationed atop the tranquil Elder Rise, Hamuul monitors disturbances across Kalimdor and confirms that the nightmare seeping through the Barrens is a dire threat demanding the full might of Horde champions.",sp=0}},faq={{q="Why does Tonga send me to Hamuul?",a="Tonga discovered that the Barrens' oases are tainted by a bizarre affliction emerging from the Wailing Caverns. Because the phenomenon feels like a nightmare gripping the earth, he sends you to Archdruid Hamuul Runetotem on Elder Rise for high-level druidic guidance before anyone attempts to enter the caverns.",al={"why hamuul","why talk to hamuul","hamuul quest purpose"},it="motive"},{q="Where is Hamuul Runetotem located?",a="Archdruid Hamuul Runetotem is located in Thunder Bluff, the capital city of the tauren in Mulgore. He stands atop the Elder Rise, overlooking the surrounding plains alongside other druids and shamans.",al={"hamuul location","where is hamuul","find hamuul runetotem"},gp=true},{q="What is the source of the taint Tonga noticed?",a="The taint stems from the underground springs of the Wailing Caverns. The strange waters are corrupting local wildlife and flora, causing the land to behave as if it is trapped in an inescapable nightmare.",al={"what is the taint","oasis corruption","wailing caverns taint"},it="threat"},{q="What happens after speaking with Hamuul?",a="Hamuul welcomes you to Thunder Bluff and prepares you for the trials ahead. He warns that dealing with the nightmare beneath the Barrens is a dire endeavor and directs you to Nara Wildmane to prepare for the descent into the Wailing Caverns.",al={"next quest after hamuul","what next","hamuul follow up"},it="next_step"},{q="Who is Hamuul Runetotem?",a="Archdruid Hamuul Runetotem is the foremost leader of the tauren druids and a close childhood friend and advisor to High Chieftain Cairne Bloodhoof. Having learned the ways of the wild following the Third War, he guides tauren druids into communion with nature and the Cenarion Circle.",al={"who is hamuul","hamuul lore","archdruid hamuul"},it="identity"},{q="Is this quest required to enter the Wailing Caverns?",a="No attunement is required to physically step into the Wailing Caverns, but this quest is the Horde narrative bridge linking the mystery of the Barrens' lush oases to the expedition inside the dungeon.",al={"wailing caverns attunement","is this quest mandatory"},gp=true},{q="Why does Tonga Runetotem ask an adventurer to go to Hamuul?",a="Tonga Runetotem is stationed in the Crossroads to actively monitor the strange, disturbing changes spreading through the Barrens and its oases. Because he must remain in the field studying the corrupted wildlife firsthand, he relies on capable travelers to carry his reports and seek guidance directly from Archdruid Hamuul Runetotem on the Elder Rise in Thunder Bluff.",al={"why send me to hamuul","why cant tonga go to hamuul","why me tonga"},it="why_me",add="a40fa735"}},ang={["class:Druid"]="For tauren druids, reporting to Archdruid Hamuul Runetotem is a pilgrimage to the mentor who established modern tauren druidism under Malfurion Stormrage's teachings.",["race:Tauren"]="The mission bridges concerns in the ancestral hunting grounds of the Barrens with the guidance of the tribal elders dwelling atop the sacred bluffs of Mulgore.",["faction:Horde"]="As the Barrens serves as the crossroad of the young Horde, investigating the spreading taint protects the supply lines connecting Durotar, Mulgore, and the northern outposts."},kw={"elder rise","hamuul runetotem","oases","taint","the barrens","thunder bluff","tonga runetotem","wailing caverns"},rel={"npc:tonga-runetotem","subzone:elder-rise","zone:thunderbluff","zone:wailing","zone:barrens","topic:druid"},m={start="Tonga Runetotem",["end"]="Archdruid Hamuul Runetotem",level="16",faction="Horde",id=1489},src={"Hamuul Runetotem (quest)"}}
E["quest:1490"] = {t="quest",n="Nara Wildmane",z="wailing",s="Nara Wildmane is a young tauren druid in Thunder Bluff seeking to unravel the tragedy unfolding deep within the Wailing Caverns. After Arch Druid Hamuul Runetotem peered into the Emerald Dream and withdrew from the corruption festering there, he dispatched adventurers to confer with Nara, whose fierce spirit endured long enough to witness the nightmare taking hold of their kin. She serves as the pivotal Horde contact directing champions to put an end to the Druids of the Fang.",h="Nara Wildmane is a young tauren druid in Thunder Bluff seeking to unravel the tragedy unfolding deep within...",sec={{t="A Vision of Corruption",b="When strange, unnatural phenomena began spreading across the Barrens, Arch Druid Hamuul Runetotem journeyed into the Emerald Dream to discern the cause. There he witnessed a cult of druids who had originally sought to restore life to the arid savannah, only to lose their minds to a vile taint. Being aged and unable to linger long against the nightmare's assault, Hamuul fled back to the waking world. However, his younger disciple, Nara Wildmane, refused to yield so easily. Her fiery resolve kept her anchored in the dreamscape far longer, allowing her to observe the transformed cult firsthand.",sp=0},{t="Confronting the Nightmare",b="While Hamuul provides the overarching guidance for the Cenarion Circle in Thunder Bluff, Nara Wildmane possesses the tactical insight needed to purge the rot. Having stared directly upon the twisted, serpent-scaled countenances of the fallen druids, she knows their crimes and the devastation they intend to unleash upon Kalimdor. Her resolve marks the beginning of the Horde's offensive into the Wailing Caverns to eliminate the leaders who abandoned their sacred oaths.",sp=1}},faq={{q="Who is Nara Wildmane?",a="Nara Wildmane is a young and spirited tauren druid residing on the Elder Rise in Thunder Bluff. She studies under Arch Druid Hamuul Runetotem and is unafraid to confront the corrupting nightmares threatening the balance of nature.",al={"who is nara","nara wildmane lore","nara wildmane thunder bluff"},it="identity"},{q="Why does Hamuul Runetotem send travelers to speak with her?",a="Hamuul admits that his advanced age and failing strength prevented him from lingering within the corrupted dream where the Druids of the Fang reside. Because Nara is young and fiercely determined, she stayed in the dreaming realm longer and gathered vital intelligence on the cult's plans.",al={"why speak with nara","hamuul to nara","why hamuul send me here"},it="motive"},{q="What did Nara see in the Emerald Dream?",a="Nara bore witness to the fallen druids dwelling in the Wailing Caverns. She saw their faces twisted into serpentine, scaled visages and perceived the dark plots and crimes they intend to enact upon the Barrens.",al={"what did nara see","nara dream vision","scaled druids dream"}},{q="Where can Nara Wildmane be found?",a="She can be found in a druidic tent situated atop the Elder Rise in Thunder Bluff, just across from Arch Druid Hamuul Runetotem.",al={"where is nara","nara wildmane location","find nara wildmane"},it="place",gp=true},{q="What happens after reporting to Nara Wildmane?",a="Once you speak with her, Nara instructs you to enter the Wailing Caverns and slay the rogue Druids of the Fang, setting up the major dungeon quest 'Leaders of the Fang'.",al={"next quest after nara","what does nara want me to do","leaders of the fang follow up"},it="next_step"},{q="Why are the druids in the Wailing Caverns corrupted?",a="Led by Naralex, the druids entered the caverns hoping to tap into the Emerald Dream and bring lush life to the Barrens. Instead, Naralex's slumber twisted into a horrific nightmare, ensnaring his followers and twisting them into the serpentine Druids of the Fang.",al={"wailing caverns cult","druids of the fang why evil","why barrens druids evil"},it="threat"},{q="Why does Hamuul Runetotem ask you to speak with Nara instead of going himself?",a="Arch Druid Hamuul Runetotem is burdened by old age and the toll of reaching into the spirit realm. When he entered the Emerald Dream to investigate the troubles in the Wailing Caverns, his strength failed, forcing him to pull back. Nara Wildmane is young and fierce, remaining in the dreaming long after he fled. Because Hamuul is in Thunder Bluff coordinating the tauren druids and cannot afford to spend what little vitality he has running errant messages or facing the threat alone, he entrusts capable travelers to learn what Nara discovered.",al={"why hamuul send me to nara","why can't hamuul speak to nara","why send an adventurer to nara"},it="why_me",add="2cdff5a8"}},ang={["race:Tauren"]="For tauren who have recently embraced the path of druidism under Hamuul, Nara represents the young, unyielding generation willing to confront unnatural blight head-on.",["class:Druid"]="Druids will appreciate Nara's courage in navigating the treacherous, corrupted reaches of the Emerald Dream where even veteran masters like Hamuul hesitated to linger.",["faction:Horde"]="Nara's vigilance protects the heart of Horde territory, ensuring that the dark energies twisting the Barrens do not spread unchecked into Mulgore."},kw={"barrens","druids of the fang","elder rise","emerald dream","hamuul runetotem","nara wildmane","thunder bluff","wailing caverns"},rel={"zone:wailing","quest:914","topic:druid","zone:barrens"},m={start="Arch Druid Hamuul Runetotem",["end"]="Nara Wildmane",level="16",faction="Horde",id=1490},src={"Nara Wildmane (quest)"}}
E["quest:1491"] = {t="quest",n="Smart Drinks",z="wailing",s="Smart Drinks is an entrepreneurial scheme cooked up by the goblin merchant Mebok Mizzyrix in Ratchet. Having failed to brew an intellect-enhancing tonic out of Sunscale raptor horns, Mebok now tasks adventurers with delving into the Wailing Caverns to harvest ectoplasmic residue for his latest beverage formula.",h="Smart Drinks is an entrepreneurial scheme cooked up by the goblin merchant Mebok Mizzyrix in Ratchet.",sec={{t="A Recipe for Disaster",b="Operating out of the bustling port town of Ratchet, Mebok Mizzyrix embodies the classic goblin philosophy of turning any bizarre regional phenomenon into cold, hard coin. Convinced that an intellect-boosting draught will make him an overnight tycoon, he originally believed powdered raptor horns held the secret. When that batch proved thoroughly underwhelming, he simply set his sights on an even more dubious ingredient: the corrupting essence seeping out of the nearby Wailing Caverns.",sp=0},{t="The Wailing Essence",b="The Barrens have experienced unsettling ecological mutations, with lush oases abruptly sprouting and local wildlife warping into aggressive horrors. Mizzyrix theorizes that a strange substance he calls 'Wailing Essence' is the catalyst behind these sudden shifts. Concluding that whatever alters biology so intensely must make a potent secret ingredient, he dispatches mercenaries to destroy the oozing ectoplasms dwelling deep within the cavern labyrinth and siphon their glowing fluid straight into beverage bottles.",sp=0}},faq={{q="Who is Mebok Mizzyrix?",a="Mebok Mizzyrix is an enterprising goblin stationed in the port town of Ratchet. Unbothered by health codes, he is obsessed with creating a commercial 'smart drink' to sell across Kalimdor and strike it rich.",al={"mebok mizzyrix","who gives smart drinks","smart drinks quest giver"},it="identity"},{q="Why didn't the raptor horns work?",a="Mebok originally believed that grinding up horns from Sunscale raptors would produce a potent intellect-boosting concoction. The resulting beverage failed to deliver the promised genius, forcing him to pivot to a far more dangerous active ingredient.",al={"why raptor horns failed","raptor horn drink"},it="history"},{q="What is Wailing Essence?",a="Wailing Essence is an ectoplasmic substance found dripping from the unnatural slimes deep inside the Wailing Caverns. Mebok believes this volatile matter is the driving catalyst behind the bizarre botanical and animal mutations spreading through the Barrens.",al={"what is wailing essence","essence from wailing caverns"},it="item"},{q="Where do you find the ectoplasms carrying the essence?",a="The essence is gathered from ectoplasmic creatures such as evolving, devouring, and nightmare ectoplasms that lurk inside the underground tunnels of the Wailing Caverns, located west of Ratchet.",al={"where are ectoplasms","smart drinks mobs","who drops wailing essence"},gp=true},{q="Is the smart drink safe to consume?",a="Considering the essence is harvested from nightmarish slimes linked to corrupting mutations across the Barrens, bottling it as a commercial tonic is wildly reckless. True to goblin business ethics, Mebok is far more concerned with marketability than customer safety.",al={"is smart drink poisonous","does the drink work"},it="power"},{q="What comes after completing Smart Drinks?",a="Smart Drinks concludes Mebok's immediate beverage venture. Satisfied with your delivery of Wailing Essence, he rewards you and promises to share future profits once his dubious tonic makes him a fortune.",al={"smart drinks follow up","what next after smart drinks"},it="next_step"},{q="Why does Mebok Mizzyrix want the Wailing Essence?",a="Mebok Mizzyrix is an ambitious goblin entrepreneur in Ratchet determined to strike it rich. After his initial attempt using raptor horns failed to produce an intellect-enhancing beverage, he pivoted to a far more volatile ingredient. Believing that the strange mutations warping the Barrens' flora and fauna stem from the potent energies within Wailing Essence, he intends to brew it directly into his concoctions and sell them as miraculous smart drinks for immense personal profit.",al={"mebok motive","why does mebok want smart drinks","why make smart drinks"},it="motive",add="b3462a0e"},{q="What are the ectoplasms carrying the essence?",a="The ectoplasms are strange, ooze-like manifestations dwelling deep within the Wailing Caverns. As volatile, corrupted energies pool beneath the oasis fissures, the local subterranean essence congeals into evolving, devouring, and nightmarish spectral slimes. These mindless entities absorb the primal, mutagenic hum of the caverns, concentrating the strange Wailing Essence inside their shifting forms until harvested.",al={"what ectoplasms","wailing caverns ectoplasm","who holds the essence"},it="target",add="6730f7d3"}},ang={["profession:Cooking"]="Any culinarian will immediately spot the health code catastrophe unfolding in Ratchet: steeping raw, nightmare-tainted ectoplasm directly into a drinkable tonic violates every standard of food safety.",["class:Druid"]="While druids enter the Wailing Caverns to cleanse the nightmare twisting the emerald dreamscape, Mebok sees the tragic ecological taint merely as cheap liquid syrup for his retail venture.",["faction:Horde"]="For travelers navigating through the crossroads of the Barrens, Ratchet's merchants offer plenty of quick coin, provided you do not ask too many questions about what they plan to do with the monster parts you deliver."},kw={"barrens","ectoplasm","mebok mizzyrix","raptor horns","ratchet","smart drinks","wailing caverns","wailing essence"},rel={"npc:mebok-mizzyrix","quest:865","zone:wailing","subzone:ratchet","zone:barrens"},m={start="Mebok Mizzyrix",level="18",id=1491,ri={"Wailing Essence"}},src={"Smart Drinks"}}
E["quest:6981"] = {t="quest",n="The Glowing Shard",z="wailing",s="The Glowing Shard is a mysterious emerald-hued gem plucked from the dark depths of the Wailing Caverns. Swirling with smoky essence beneath its polished surface, this disturbing relic drives adventurers to seek answers in Ratchet and beyond.",h="The Glowing Shard is a mysterious emerald-hued gem plucked from the dark depths of the Wailing Caverns.",sec={{t="A Disturbing Discovery",b="Drawn from deep within the Wailing Caverns, the glowing shard immediately unnerves those who hold it. Brilliant green and seemingly solid, it holds churning, mist-like shadows beneath its crystalline face. The crystal exerts a subtle pull, demanding attention while exuding a deeply unsettling aura that hints at the corrupted nature of the slumbering druids and their nightmare-infested sanctuary.",sp=0},{t="Seeking Answers in Ratchet",b="Uncertain of the stone's origin or nature, adventurers bring the artifact to the goblin port of Ratchet. There, local engineer Sputtervalve inspects the oddity, only to recognize that its origins lie beyond the scope of goblin machinery and standard geology. Instead, he directs seekers up into the rocky ridges above the caverns, where the tauren mystic Falla Sagewind watches over the troubled spirits of the Barrens.",sp=1}},faq={{q="What is the Glowing Shard?",a="It is a corrupted, luminescent green crystal found deep within the Wailing Caverns. Inside its glassy shell, faint smoke swirls, unsettling anyone who studies it closely.",al={"glowing shard item","what is this green gem","shard from wailing caverns"},it="item"},{q="Who can examine the shard in Ratchet?",a="Sputtervalve, an engineer stationed near the flight master in Ratchet, examines the shard. Though he is an engineer rather than a druid, he recognizes its strange energy and points you toward someone with spiritual expertise.",al={"who in ratchet looks at shard","ratchet npc for shard","sputtervalve shard"},it="purpose",gp=true},{q="Where is Falla Sagewind located?",a="Falla Sagewind makes her camp on the mountain peaks directly above the entrance to the Wailing Caverns in the central Barrens.",al={"falla sagewind location","where is falla","mountain above wailing caverns"},it="target",gp=true},{q="Does Sputtervalve have a quest marker over his head?",a="No. Sputtervalve does not display an active quest icon. You must speak with him directly and select the dialogue prompt regarding the strange glowing shard to advance.",al={"sputtervalve no question mark","cant turn in to sputtervalve","sputtervalve bugged"},gp=true},{q="Why does the shard look like it contains smoke?",a="The smoky swirl within the crystal reflects the pervasive corruption warping the Wailing Caverns, tied directly to the Emerald Nightmare invading the thoughts of the slumbering Druids of the Fang.",al={"why does shard smoke","green smoke in gem","corruption in shard"},it="power"},{q="Who can complete the quest chain after Falla Sagewind?",a="Both Horde and Alliance adventurers can pursue this storyline. Falla Sagewind's findings lead directly into the quest 'In Nightmares', sending heroes to seek guidance from their respective leaders and elders.",al={"is this quest horde only","alliance glowing shard","who gets in nightmares"},sp=1,it="next_step",gp=true},{q="Why do you need to investigate the Glowing Shard?",a="The glowing shard is deeply unsettling. Solid yet filled with swirling, smoky green depths, it exudes an unnatural presence that demands explanation. Having recovered it from the heart of the troubled Wailing Caverns, you need to understand what corruption it carries and what threat it might pose to the Barrens.",al={"why investigate the glowing shard","glowing shard motive","why take the shard to ratchet"},it="motive",add="8f9c92be"}},ang={["class:Druid"]="For druids, the shard's emerald sheen and smoky core are grim evidence of the Emerald Nightmare seeping into the waking world through their fallen brethren in the Wailing Caverns.",["race:Tauren"]="The balance of the Barrens is dear to the Shu'halo, and bringing this unnatural relic to Falla Sagewind aids in understanding the corruption poisoning their ancestral lands.",["faction:Horde"]="Unraveling the mystery of the shard helps protect the vital crossroads and trade routes of the Barrens from unnatural threats festering in the underground springs.",["faction:Alliance"]="Even far from home in Kalimdor, Alliance explorers recognize the global peril posed by whatever dark power is corrupting nature beneath the Barrens."},kw={"barrens","druids of the fang","emerald nightmare","falla sagewind","glowing shard","ratchet","sputtervalve","wailing caverns"},rel={"zone:wailing","npc:sputtervalve","npc:falla-sagewind","quest:3369","subzone:ratchet","topic:goblin","topic:horde","topic:alliance"},m={start="Glowing Shard",["end"]="Falla Sagewind",level="26",id=6981},src={"The Glowing Shard"}}
E["quest:914"] = {t="quest",n="Leaders of the Fang",z="wailing",s="Leaders of the Fang is a pivotal Horde quest tasked by Nara Wildmane from the heights of Thunder Bluff. It directs adventurers into the Wailing Caverns to strike down the four leaders of the corrupted Druids of the Fang and retrieve their twisted dream gems. Halting these rogue druids is essential to preventing their serpentine nightmare from permanently overtaking the Barrens.",h="Leaders of the Fang is a pivotal Horde quest tasked by Nara Wildmane from the heights of Thunder Bluff.",sec={{t="A Vision Corrupted",b="The night elf archdruid Naralex ventured into the subterranean springs of the Wailing Caverns with a selfless ambition: to use the Emerald Dream to restore lush vitality to the arid Barrens. Tragically, when his slumber took root, his dream turned into a waking nightmare. The acolytes who accompanied him lost their devotion to nature's harmony, succumbing to malignant serpent spirits and adopting the mantle of the Druids of the Fang.",sp=0},{t="The Four Dream Gems",b="To reshape the Barrens into their own viperous Eden, the leaders of the splintered sect channel the warped dream energies through specialized foci known as dream gems. Lord Cobrahn, Lady Anacondra, Lord Pythas, and Lord Serpentis each bear one of these gems. As long as these artifacts remain in their grasp, their corrupting influence will seep outward into the soil and waters of Kalimdor.",sp=0},{t="A Burden Lifted in Thunder Bluff",b="Nara Wildmane, watching over the natural balance from Thunder Bluff, feels the spiritual torment rippling from the caverns directly into her mind. By hunting down the four serpent lords and stripping them of their gems, Horde champions break the sect's command structure, freeing the tauren druid from lingering nightmares and saving the surrounding plains from an unnatural blight.",sp=1}},faq={{q="Who are the leaders of the Druids of the Fang?",a="The sect is guided by four fallen druids: Lady Anacondra, Lord Cobrahn, Lord Pythas, and Lord Serpentis. Each has surrendered their original nature teachings to embody serpent forms and channel nightmare magic within the Wailing Caverns.",al={"leaders of the fang names","wailing caverns bosses","who leads druids of the fang"},it="target"},{q="What are the dream gems?",a="The dream gems are conduits carried by each of the four leaders within the Wailing Caverns. They focus the twisted, nightmare-tainted energy leaking from Naralex's slumber, fueling the sect's efforts to mutate the Barrens.",al={"what are the gems","gem of cobrahn","dream gems lore"},it="item"},{q="Why does Nara Wildmane want the gems?",a="Nara Wildmane is a tauren druid in Thunder Bluff who feels the psychic and spiritual ripples of the nightmare. The faces of the corrupted leaders haunt her dreams, and she needs their power broken to protect both her sanity and the future of the Barrens.",al={"who is nara wildmane","why kill the leaders","nara wildmane motive"},it="why_wanted"},{q="Were the Druids of the Fang always evil?",a="No. They were originally noble night elf druids who followed Naralex into the caverns hoping to heal the dry savanna. When Naralex fell into a nightmare, the energies warped their minds, transforming them into a fanatical snake cult.",al={"druids of the fang origin","why did the druids turn bad","naralex disciples"},it="history"},{q="Where is this quest turned in?",a="The quest begins and ends with Nara Wildmane on the Elder Rise in Thunder Bluff. Once you collect all four gems from the depths of the Wailing Caverns, you must travel back to Mulgore to present them to her.",al={"leaders of the fang turn in","where is nara wildmane","hand in leaders of the fang"},gp=true},{q="Does killing the leaders cure Naralex?",a="Slaying the four leaders shatters the sect's upper hierarchy and stops the spread of their ritual, but it does not wake Naralex on its own. Other druidic rites deeper within the caverns are required to awaken the slumbering master.",al={"does this save naralex","killing leaders effect"}},{q="Why does Nara Wildmane want the Druids of the Fang killed?",a="The Druids of the Fang are former Cenarion Circle druids who set out to restore the lushness of the Barrens, but their minds became warped by the Emerald Nightmare. Now they seek to remake the land into their own twisted dreamscape. Their corruption plagues Nara's own thoughts and dreams, and she fears that unless their four leaders are slain and their influence broken, the entire Barrens will fall to a dark and cursed future.",al={"nara wildmane motive","why kill druids of the fang","why does nara want them dead"},it="motive",add="5ca16cf2"}},ang={["class:Druid"]="For tauren druids, this mission is deeply personal. Seeing fellow servants of nature twist the Emerald Dream into a poisonous blight is an intolerable affront to Cenarion principles.",["faction:Horde"]="The Barrens is the vital crossroads connecting Orgrimmar, Thunder Bluff, and the Darkspear isles. Allowing a fanatical sect of serpent worshipers to mutate the land threatens the stability of the entire Horde.",["race:Tauren"]="The Earth Mother's health is central to tauren faith, making the unnatural corruption bleeding from the springs of the Barrens a direct sacrilege against the land they roam."},kw={"anacondra","barrens","cobrahn","dream gems","leaders of the fang","nara wildmane","pythas","serpentis","wailing caverns"},rel={"zone:wailing","topic:druids-of-the-fang","quest:1490","zone:barrens","zone:thunderbluff","topic:druid"},m={start="Nara Wildmane",level="22",faction="Horde",id=914,ri={"Gem of Anacondra","Gem of Cobrahn","Gem of Pythas","Gem of Serpentis"}},src={"Leaders of the Fang"}}
E["quest:959"] = {t="quest",n="Trouble at the Docks",z="wailing",s="Crane Operator Bigglefuzz caused a clumsy cargo accident on the Ratchet docks, allowing a petty troublemaker named Mad Magglish to snatch a priceless vintage bottle. The vintage—a 99-Year-Old Port sent directly from Baron Revilgaz to Gazlowe—must be recovered from the shadows of the Wailing Caverns before the dockmaster fires the negligent crane operator.",h="Crane Operator Bigglefuzz caused a clumsy cargo accident on the Ratchet docks, allowing a petty troublemaker...",sec={{t="A Clumsy Mishap",b="Ratchet thrives on constant sea trade with Booty Bay across the Great Sea, but its goblin efficiency occasionally cracks under sheer volume. When an unusually massive morning shipment arrived at the port, Crane Operator Bigglefuzz tried to cut corners to speed up the unloading process. Lifting far more than his crane could manage, he dropped the entire haul across the docks. In the ensuing chaos, a local nuisance named Mad Magglish took advantage of the spilled crates, snatched a single valuable bottle of liquor, and fled inland.",sp=0},{t="Diplomatic Vintage",b="The stolen cargo was far more than an ordinary ration of dockside spirits. The bottle was a 99-Year-Old Port sent as a personal diplomatic gift from Baron Revilgaz, the notorious Blackwater ruler of Booty Bay, to Gazlowe, the chief engineer and overseer of Ratchet. Losing such a lavish offering threatens to humiliate Bigglefuzz and enrage both trade moguls. Faced with losing his job or worse, Bigglefuzz tracked the thief to the ominous mouth of the Wailing Caverns, though fear kept him from following Magglish inside.",sp=0},{t="The Cavern Hideout",b="Rather than venturing deep into the corrupted dreamscape of the dungeon itself, Mad Magglish chose to hide within the sprawling, damp natural tunnels outside the inner gateway. Relying on clumsy stealth and dark alcoves, Magglish skulks through the subterranean caverns hoping pursuers will give up. Retrieving the port requires flushing out the thief from the outer reaches before the vintage is uncorked or destroyed.",sp=0}},faq={{q="Why is this bottle of port so important?",a="The 99-Year-Old Port is not ordinary grog; it is an extravagant personal gift sent by Baron Revilgaz of Booty Bay to Gazlowe, the boss of Ratchet. Losing it in a dock mishap threatens to deeply anger Ratchet's leadership and cost Crane Operator Bigglefuzz his livelihood.",al={"why does bigglefuzz care","what is the 99-year-old port","why is the wine important"},it="item"},{q="Who is Mad Magglish?",a="Mad Magglish is an opportunistic thief and troublemaker hanging around Ratchet. When Bigglefuzz dropped a massive cargo load on the docks, Magglish grabbed the rare bottle of port and fled straight into the nearby Wailing Caverns to hide.",al={"who is magglish","who stole the port","mad magglish lore"},it="target"},{q="Do I have to enter the Wailing Caverns dungeon to find the thief?",a="No. Mad Magglish hides in the winding, public cave passages outside the instance portal. He uses weak stealth and lurks in the upper side tunnels or near the flooded chambers leading toward the main entrance.",al={"is magglish inside the instance","where is mad magglish","find magglish"},gp=true},{q="How did the cargo spill happen?",a="A massive cargo shipment arrived from Booty Bay, and Crane Operator Bigglefuzz tried to unload more crates at once than his equipment could handle. The overloaded crane dropped the haul, scattering valuable freight across the Ratchet docks.",al={"why did the crates drop","what did bigglefuzz do","crane mishap ratchet"},it="origin"},{q="What is the relationship between Ratchet and Booty Bay?",a="Both port towns are vital strongholds of the Steamwheedle Cartel, bound by commerce and privateer fleets. Regular trade shipments and formal courtesies pass between Baron Revilgaz in the south and Gazlowe in the Barrens to maintain their mutual trade empire.",al={"ratchet and booty bay connection","steamwheedle ports","revilgaz and gazlowe"},it="ties"},{q="Why didn't Bigglefuzz retrieve the bottle himself?",a="Bigglefuzz pursued the thief right to the entrance of the Wailing Caverns, but the eerie reputation and monstrous inhabitants of the underground labyrinth terrified the goblin into stopping at the threshold.",al={"why didn't the goblin get it","why did bigglefuzz stop chasing"},it="why_me"},{q="Why does Crane Operator Bigglefuzz need this port back?",a="Bigglefuzz's job is on the line. When he tried to unload more crates than his crane could handle, the entire morning shipment from Booty Bay collapsed. In the chaos, the prized bottle of ninety-nine-year-old port went missing, and the dockmaster has been breathing down his neck ever since. Because the vintage was a personal gift meant for Ratchet's chief engineer, Gazlowe, failing to recover it means Bigglefuzz is facing immediate dismissal.",al={"why does bigglefuzz want the port","bigglefuzz motive","why help bigglefuzz"},it="motive",add="b908c2b9"}},ang={["class:Rogue"]="Hunting Mad Magglish is an exercise in spotting sloppy concealment, as the thief relies on rudimentary stealth within the cavern crannies to escape notice.",["faction:Horde"]="Assisting Ratchet's dockhands helps maintain smooth operations for the primary neutral port connecting Kalimdor to the Eastern Kingdoms.",["faction:Alliance"]="Though operating deep within the Horde-dominated Barrens, staying on the good side of Steamwheedle port operators ensures safe passage through neutral waters."},kw={"bigglefuzz","booty bay","gazlowe","magglish","port","ratchet","revilgaz","wailing caverns"},rel={"npc:crane-operator-bigglefuzz","subzone:ratchet","zone:wailing","npc:baron-revilgaz","subzone:booty-bay","zone:barrens"},m={start="Crane Operator Bigglefuzz",level="18",id=959,ri={"99-Year-Old Port"}},src={"Trouble at the Docks"}}
E["quest:962"] = {t="quest",n="Serpentbloom",z="wailing",s="Serpentbloom is a gathering task issued by Apothecary Zamah, an envoy of the Royal Apothecary Society residing in Thunder Bluff. Zamah seeks specimens of a rare herb native to the subterranean depths of the Wailing Caverns to aid the research of the Forsaken.",h="Serpentbloom is a gathering task issued by Apothecary Zamah, an envoy of the Royal Apothecary Society...",sec={{t="Eyes of the Apothecary",b="Perched upon the Spirit Rise in Thunder Bluff, Apothecary Zamah serves as an envoy of the Royal Apothecary Society from the Undercity. While the tauren hosts focus on spiritual balance and healing the wounded land, Zamah's attention is fixed on rare and virulent materials. Having isolated a sample of an unusual plant known as Serpentbloom, she seeks bulk quantities to advance the research directives of Lady Sylvanas Windrunner and the Forsaken.",sp=0},{t="The Depths of the Caverns",b="Serpentbloom does not grow under the open sun of the Barrens, thriving instead in the damp, twisting grottos of the Wailing Caverns. Cultivated in the humid subterranean climate twisted by the corrupted druids of the Fang, the plant is difficult to reach and fiercely guarded by the cavern's serpentine denizens. Zamah readily admits that numerous scouts sent before failed to return, leaving further harvesting to hardened adventurers.",sp=0}},faq={{q="Who is Apothecary Zamah?",a="Apothecary Zamah is a researcher representing the Royal Apothecary Society of the Undercity. Stationed in Thunder Bluff on the Spirit Rise, she acts as a liaison between the Forsaken alchemists and the wider continent of Kalimdor.",al={"zamah","apothecary zamah lore","who gives serpentbloom"},it="identity"},{q="Why does the Royal Apothecary Society want Serpentbloom?",a="Zamah believes the herb possesses significant latent chemical potential when refined in large quantities. The Society actively searches across Kalimdor for rare, potent flora that can aid the Forsaken's alchemical experiments.",al={"why serpentbloom","forsaken herb research","purpose of serpentbloom"},it="item"},{q="Where does Serpentbloom grow?",a="Serpentbloom grows exclusively inside the subterranean reaches of the Wailing Caverns, nestled within the damp rock corridors and subterranean passages carved beneath the northern Barrens.",al={"where is serpentbloom","serpentbloom location"},it="place",gp=true},{q="Why haven't previous scouts returned?",a="The Wailing Caverns are overrun by devolved beasts, raptors, and the corrupted Druids of the Fang. Less experienced foragers sent into the labyrinthian tunnels were quickly overwhelmed by the cavern's predatory fauna and venomous defenders.",al={"missing scouts","zamah's scouts","is wailing caverns dangerous"},it="threat"},{q="Do the Tauren approve of Zamah's research?",a="The tauren of Thunder Bluff granted the Forsaken sanctuary out of sympathy and a desire to heal them, but the alchemical practices of the Royal Apothecary Society often skirt close to unnatural experimentation that makes traditional shamans and druids uneasy.",al={"tauren reaction","spirit rise apothecaries"},it="conflict"},{q="Does harvesting Serpentbloom require herbalism skills?",a="No. While it is a botanical specimen, any adventurer willing to brave the depths of the Wailing Caverns can pluck the plants directly from the cave floor without formal herbalism training.",al={"do i need herbalism","gather serpentbloom profession"},gp=true},{q="Why does Apothecary Zamah want Serpentbloom gathered?",a="Apothecary Zamah was dispatched to Thunder Bluff by the Royal Apothecary Society on a specific assignment to further the interests of the Forsaken and the Dark Lady, Lady Sylvanas Windrunner. Having analyzed a rare sample of Serpentbloom, Zamah sees immense potential in its properties if obtained in substantial quantities. Securing enough specimens allows her research to advance the scientific and alchemical ambitions of the Undercity.",al={"apothecary zamah motive","why does zamah need serpentbloom","why gather serpentbloom"},it="motive",add="962715c8"},{q="Why does Apothecary Zamah send an adventurer instead of gathering Serpentbloom herself?",a="Zamah cannot easily abandon her station in Thunder Bluff, and harvesting the herb requires venturing into the treacherous, corrupted depths of the Wailing Caverns. She has already dispatched several scouts and agents into the cave system on her behalf, but none of them returned alive. She needs seasoned, capable adventurers willing to brave those dark recesses where ordinary scouts failed.",al={"why send me serpentbloom","why doesn't zamah get serpentbloom","why adventurers for serpentbloom"},it="why_me",add="92b49307"}},ang={["race:Undead"]="Contributing Serpentbloom directly supports the Royal Apothecary Society's alchemical initiatives in Lordaeron under the Dark Lady's mandate.",["race:Tauren"]="Hosting Forsaken apothecaries upon the Spirit Rise reflects the Horde's hospitality, even as their focus on lethal concoctions contrasts with traditional earth healing.",["profession:Herbalism"]="The twisted environment inside the Wailing Caverns fosters unique flora found nowhere else on the sunbaked surface of the Barrens.",["faction:Horde"]="This task cements the early operational alliance between the Undercity and the Kalimdor tribes, sharing resources and rare reagents across the ocean."},kw={"apothecary","barrens","royal apothecary society","serpentbloom","spirit rise","thunder bluff","undercity","wailing caverns","zamah"},rel={"quest:853","topic:royal-apothecary-society","zone:wailing","zone:thunderbluff","topic:forsaken","zone:undercity","zone:barrens"},m={start="Apothecary Zamah",level="18",faction="Horde",id=962,ri={"Serpentbloom"}},src={"Serpentbloom (quest)"}}
E["subzone:cavern-of-mists"] = {t="subzone",n="Cavern of Mists",z="wailing",s="The Cavern of Mists is the expansive outer antechamber leading into the depths of the Wailing Caverns. Fed by subterranean geysers that erupt through the rock, its central pool and hanging fog harbor strange, mutated wildlife roaming just outside the portal threshold.",h="The Cavern of Mists is the expansive outer antechamber leading into the depths of the Wailing Caverns.",sec={{t="The Threshold of the Nightmare",b="Before descending into the true heart of the Wailing Caverns, travelers must navigate the Cavern of Mists. Thick, warm vapor hangs permanently in the air, fed by natural geysers erupting from the cavern floor into a deep central pool. Though it serves as an entryway, it is far from peaceful. Swarms of raptors, serpents, oozes, and semi-aquatic threshadons wander the ledges and waters, alongside notorious beasts like the hydra Trigore the Lasher. It provides adventurers an ominous preview of the unnatural growth festering deeper below.",sp=0}},faq={{q="Where is the Cavern of Mists?",a="The Cavern of Mists comprises the outer cave system of the Wailing Caverns, located southwest of the Crossroads in the Barrens. It is the non-instanced chamber that players must traverse to reach the instance portal itself.",al={"cavern of mists location","where is cavern of mists","wailing caverns entrance cave"},it="place",gp=true},{q="Why is it called the Cavern of Mists?",a="Active geysers constantly burst from the stone floor, feeding the central pool and filling the subterranean air with heavy, humid fog.",al={"why misty","cavern of mists name origin"},it="name"},{q="What creatures live here?",a="The chamber is populated by raptors, oozes, wind serpents, snakes, toads, and threshadons inhabiting the pool, as well as occasional sightings of the rare hydra Trigore the Lasher.",al={"mobs in cavern of mists","cavern of mists monsters"},it="residents"},{q="Who is Trigore the Lasher?",a="Trigore the Lasher is a dangerous rare hydra that can occasionally be found swimming alongside the threshadons in the chamber's central pool.",al={"trigore","hydra rare wailing caverns"}},{q="What is the Cavern of Mists?",a="The Cavern of Mists, also referred to as the Wailing Cavern, is the outer subterranean chamber preceding the deeper reaches of the Wailing Caverns. Fed by active geysers that erupt from the stone floor, the cavern features a verdant central pool where warm water and vapor mingle, filling the enclosed subterranean air with a perpetual, heavy fog.",al={"what is cavern of mists","cavern of mists lore","about cavern of mists"},it="place",add="923aae57"},{q="Is the Cavern of Mists dangerous?",a="Yes, the chamber is perilous for unwary travelers. Wild predators prowl the misty banks and murky waters, including aggressive raptors, creeping oozes, venomous snakes, and snapping wind serpents. The deep central pool is home to predatory threshadons, alongside monstrous threats such as the elusive hydra known as Trigore the Lasher.",al={"is cavern of mists dangerous","cavern of mists danger","threats in cavern of mists"},it="danger",add="8ec0c6f8"}},ang={["class:Druid"]="The twisted wildlife thriving in the heavy vapors gives Cenarion druids their first warning of how deeply Naralex's Emerald Dream communion has gone astray.",["faction:Horde"]="Resting right in the heart of the Barrens, clearing out the predatory beasts lurking in these mists is critical to securing the trade routes and outposts around the Crossroads."},kw={"barrens","cavern of mists","geysers","threshadons","trigore the lasher","wailing caverns"},rel={"zone:wailing","quest:938"},src={"Cavern of Mists"}}
E["subzone:crag-of-the-everliving"] = {t="subzone",n="Crag of the Everliving",z="wailing",s="The Crag of the Everliving is a verdant cavern chamber nestled deep within the Wailing Caverns. Dominated by lush, corrupted flora and predatory plant creatures, it serves as the domain of the Fanglord Lord Pythas. Its towering upper reaches shelter the ancient entity after whom the crag is named.",h="The Crag of the Everliving is a verdant cavern chamber nestled deep within the Wailing Caverns.",sec={{t="A Corrupted Canopy",b="While much of the Wailing Caverns is carved of damp subterranean stone, the Crag of the Everliving bursts with unruly, twisted vegetation fueled by the Nightmare corrupting Naralex's slumber. Towering mossy platforms and winding paths are choked with Deviate Shamblers—living plant hulks prowling the undergrowth. Lord Pythas, one of Naralex's fallen disciples, watches over the crag's central reaches, having traded his noble druidic vows for the venomous rites of the Druids of the Fang.",sp=0},{t="The Ancient Guardian",b="The chamber draws its name from Verdan the Everliving, a colossal, primordial plant elemental who resides in the crag's upper heights. Corrupted by the Emerald Nightmare that grips the cavern, Verdan now acts as a fearsome line of defense rather than a peaceful natural guardian. Beyond his towering form lurks Lord Serpentis, the self-proclaimed chief of the Fanglords, who oversees the sect's descent into serpentine madness.",sp=0}},faq={{q="Where does this area get its name?",a="The chamber is named after Verdan the Everliving, an ancient and colossal plant beast residing in the highest terraces of the crag. Though once an embodiment of nature's timeless vitality, he has fallen under the sway of the Nightmare that afflicts the caverns.",al={"why crag of the everliving","everliving name origin","crag name"},it="name"},{q="Who controls this part of the caverns?",a="Lord Pythas, one of the primary Fanglords, directly presides over the crag. In the higher ledges above him lurk both Verdan the Everliving and Lord Serpentis, the leader of the Druids of the Fang.",al={"who is in charge here","crag boss","fanglord here"},it="in_charge"},{q="What creatures are commonly found in the Crag of the Everliving?",a="The crag is overrun with Deviate Shamblers—shambling plant horrors birthed from the corrupted springs—alongside twisted serpents and the fanatical Druids of the Fang.",al={"monsters in crag","crag enemies","what lives here"},it="residents"},{q="Why is plant life thriving so deep underground?",a="The underground springs were harnessed by the night elf druid Naralex to rejuvenate the Barrens. When his ritual was snared by the Emerald Nightmare, the wild growth ran rampant and twisted into hostile, aberrant flora.",al={"why are there plants underground","why so green","corrupted greenery"},it="origin"},{q="What is the Crag of the Everliving?",a="The Crag of the Everliving is a lush, verdant subterranean cavern deep within the Wailing Caverns. Fed by corrupted natural energies, it is characterized by flourishing plant life, rampant growth, and towering rock shelves.",al={"what is crag of the everliving","crag of the everliving info","about crag of the everliving"},it="place",add="6a6b08ee"},{q="Is the Crag of the Everliving dangerous?",a="Yes, it is among the deadliest portions of the caverns. Deviate Shamblers stalk the overgrown terraces, and the crag is defended by corrupted druids of the Fang, presided over by Lord Pythas and near the lair of Lord Serpentis.",al={"how dangerous is crag of the everliving","is crag of the everliving dangerous","threats in crag of the everliving"},it="danger",add="cca8a755"}},ang={["class:Druid"]="Seeing the Crag of the Everliving is a tragic lesson for Cenarion druids, as pure natural vitality and elemental guardianship have been warped into lethal tools of the Nightmare.",["profession:Herbalism"]="The crag's unnaturally lush subterranean atmosphere nourishes rare underground roots and mushrooms that flourish in the humid, dream-soaked soil."},kw={"barrens","crag of the everliving","deviate shamblers","druids of the fang","lord pythas","lord serpentis","verdan","wailing caverns"},rel={"zone:wailing","npc:lord-pythas","npc:verdan-the-everliving","npc:lord-serpentis"},src={"Crag of the Everliving"}}
E["subzone:dreamer-s-rock"] = {t="subzone",n="Dreamer's Rock",z="wailing",s="Dreamer's Rock is a secluded natural sanctuary tucked deep within the Wailing Caverns past the Screaming Gully. Here lies the sleeping night elf druid Naralex, whose noble effort to revive the Barrens has instead birthed a living nightmare. It serves as both a sacred barrow chamber and the epicenter of the corruption mutating the surrounding subterranean ecosystem.",h="Dreamer's Rock is a secluded natural sanctuary tucked deep within the Wailing Caverns past the Screaming...",sec={{t="The Slumber of Naralex",b="Located in the heart of the Wailing Caverns, Dreamer's Rock functions much like an improvised barrow den. Here, the night elf druid Naralex entered a deep trance to tap the underground springs and channel the Emerald Dream into the arid soil of the Barrens. Instead of bringing life, his connection was seized by dark forces. The nightmare twisting his thoughts now spills physically into this chamber, twisting the local wildlife, turning his followers into the venomous Druids of the Fang, and manifesting terrifying aberrations into the waking world.",sp=0},{t="The Awakening Ritual",b="Only by ending the corruption of the Fanglords can a surviving Disciple of Naralex venture to Dreamer's Rock to perform the ritual of waking. The process is fraught with peril: as the chant begins, Naralex's lingering nightmare manifests monstrosities to defend its hold over his sleeping mind. The ultimate culmination of this psychic torment is Mutanus the Devourer, a vile aberration that materializes directly from the depths of the dreamer's subconscious to consume all who seek to free him.",sp=1}},faq={{q="Who is sleeping at Dreamer's Rock?",a="Naralex, a powerful night elf druid, lies in slumber here. He came to the Wailing Caverns hoping to harness its subterranean water channels to restore lush life to the Barrens, but his communion with the Emerald Dream was hijacked by terrible nightmares.",al={"sleeping elf","who is asleep here","who is naralex","dreamer identity"},it="residents"},{q="Why is this chamber called Dreamer's Rock?",a="The chamber is named for Naralex himself, 'the Dreamer.' Acting much like a traditional night elf barrow den, it provides the physical resting place for his body while his spirit traverses the Dream.",al={"why dreamers rock","dreamers rock name meaning","name origin"},it="name"},{q="What happens when you try to wake Naralex?",a="A surviving Disciple of Naralex attempts an awakening ritual after the Fanglords have been defeated. The outcome and manifestations encountered during the ritual are revealed when it is performed.",al={"waking naralex","disciple ritual","naralex event"},sp=1,it="next_step"},{q="Why did Naralex's followers turn hostile?",a="As Naralex's communion turned into a nightmare, the dark visions warped the minds of his acolytes. Abandoning their Cenarion vows, they embraced serpent aspects, becoming the Druids of the Fang and zealously defending their master's tormented, unending sleep.",al={"druids of the fang origin","why are the druids evil","corrupted druids"},it="conflict"},{q="What is Dreamer's Rock?",a="Dreamer's Rock is a secluded natural chamber deep within the Wailing Caverns, lying beyond the Screaming Gully. Functioning much like a traditional druidic barrow den, it serves as the resting site where the night elf druid Naralex entered his deep slumber to channel the Emerald Dream into the Barrens.",al={"what is dreamers rock","dreamers rock chamber","where is dreamers rock"},it="place",add="8278540a"},{q="What happened at Dreamer's Rock?",a="Naralex came to this chamber to tap into the Emerald Dream and restore verdant life to the arid Barrens. Instead, a dark corruption seeped into his vision, twisting his noble slumber into a waking nightmare. The horrors from his disturbed mind manifested into flesh and broke free into the cavern, corrupting his followers and the surrounding springs.",al={"dreamers rock history","what happened to naralex here","how did dreamers rock fall"},it="history",add="29a7d0a7"},{q="Is Dreamer's Rock dangerous?",a="It is exceptionally dangerous. The chamber sits at the heart of the cavern's corruption, directly exposed to Naralex's twisted subconscious. Any attempt to disturb or awaken the sleeping druid draws forth malevolent nightmare aberrations eager to keep him ensnared, including the monstrous horror known as Mutanus the Devourer.",al={"how dangerous is dreamers rock","dreamers rock threats","is it safe at dreamers rock"},sp=1,it="danger",add="70f268b5"}},ang={["class:Druid"]="Dreamer's Rock stands as a grim warning of the dangers lurking within the Emerald Dream, showing how easily noble intentions can be subverted by slumbering horrors.",["race:NightElf"]="Finding a sacred barrow-style resting chamber corrupted beneath the arid Barrens is a somber reminder of the tragic risks Naralex and his followers took far from Kalimdor's northern forests."},kw={"barrow den","dreamer's rock","dreamers rock","druids of the fang","emerald dream","mutanus","naralex","wailing caverns"},rel={"npc:naralex","zone:wailing","npc:mutanus-the-devourer","subzone:screaming-gully","topic:druid","topic:night-elf"},src={"Dreamer's Rock"}}
E["subzone:screaming-gully"] = {t="subzone",n="Screaming Gully",z="wailing",s="Screaming Gully is the first sprawling subterranean cavern encountered just beyond the entrance of the Wailing Caverns. Bathed in unnatural fungal glow and shallow waters, it serves as the outer redoubt for the corrupted Druids of the Fang and their mutated beasts.",h="Screaming Gully is the first sprawling subterranean cavern encountered just beyond the entrance of the...",sec={{t="Threshold of the Nightmare",b="Stepping through the threshold of the Wailing Caverns leads directly into Screaming Gully, an echoing chasm where the wind groans through subterranean fissures. Far from the arid Barrens above, the gully is choked with damp overgrowth, humid mist, and aggressive wildlife twisted by the Emerald Nightmare. The Fanglord Lady Anacondra oversees the chamber, surrounded by acolytes of the Druids of the Fang and vicious deviate raptors, while ancient snapping turtles like Kresh patrol the shallow waterways below.",sp=0}},faq={{q="Where is the Screaming Gully located?",a="The Screaming Gully is the first major chamber you enter directly after stepping through the portal inside the Wailing Caverns, located beneath the northern Barrens.",al={"screaming gully location","where is screaming gully","how to find screaming gully"},it="place",gp=true},{q="Why is it called the Screaming Gully?",a="The Wailing Caverns earn their name from the howling, moaning sounds caused by subterranean steam and winds venting through rock fissures, and this wide entrance chasm catches the brunt of those echoing cries.",al={"why screaming gully","screaming gully name origin"},it="name"},{q="Who rules over the Screaming Gully?",a="The chamber is overseen by Lady Anacondra, one of the primary Fanglords who fell under the corruption of the Emerald Nightmare alongside Naralex.",al={"screaming gully boss","who is in screaming gully","screaming gully leader"},it="residents"},{q="What creatures roam this chamber?",a="The gully is populated by deviate raptors, corrupted Druids of the Fang, and wandering aquatic life, including the ancient turtle Kresh roaming the flooded floor.",al={"screaming gully mobs","enemies in screaming gully"},it="danger"},{q="What is the Screaming Gully?",a="The Screaming Gully is the first sprawling subterranean chamber encountered just beyond the threshold of the Wailing Caverns. Fed by underground streams that pool into shallow waters along its floor, this cavernous rift echoes with eerie natural sounds and the hiss of corrupted wildlife, serving as the front line of the nightmare taking root within the depths.",al={"what is screaming gully","screaming gully overview","screaming gully lore"},it="place",add="edd75ba3"}},ang={["class:Druid"]="For Cenarion druids, Screaming Gully is a heartbreaking display of their fallen brethren who abandoned the path of the claw and sky to embrace serpentine corruption."},kw={"barrens","deviate raptor","fanglords","kresh","lady anacondra","screaming gully","wailing caverns"},rel={"zone:wailing","npc:lady-anacondra","topic:druids-of-the-fang","topic:druid"},src={"Screaming Gully"}}
E["zone:wailing"] = {t="dungeon",n="Wailing Caverns",z="wailing",s="Tucked beneath the Lushwater Oasis in the arid Barrens lies the Wailing Caverns, a labyrinthine system of subterranean springs and fissures named for the eerie whistling of trapped steam. What began as a noble druidic effort to revitalize Kalimdor's sun-bleached savanna has devolved into a warped, poisonous underworld. The caverns now teem with twisted wildlife and fallen disciples corrupted by a deep, unnatural nightmare.",h="Tucked beneath the Lushwater Oasis in the arid Barrens lies the Wailing Caverns, a labyrinthine system of...",sec={{t="A Noble Vision Turned Poisonous",b="The night elf druid Naralex originally discovered this vast water system and devised an ambitious design: by opening a conduit straight into the Emerald Dream, he would siphon pure primal life essence through the subterranean springs, transforming the parched Barrens back into a thriving, verdant paradise. Deep within the caverns, Naralex slipped into communion with the Dream, anchored by his loyal acolytes. Tragically, rather than tapping into pure vitality, the druid's sleeping mind touched the Emerald Nightmare. The festering corruption instantly seized him, transforming his well-intentioned conduit into a valve pouring venom and madness into the underground waterways.",sp=0},{t="The Druids of the Fang",b="As the Nightmare's dark energy radiated from Naralex's helpless form, his students succumbed to the madness. Forsaking the tranquil wisdom of the Cenarion Circle, they formed the fanatical Druids of the Fang. Taking reptilian forms, the sect's leaders—Lady Anacondra, Lord Cobrahn, Lord Pythas, and Lord Serpentis—now embrace the venomous mutation of the caverns rather than fighting it. They actively shield their sleeping master from any outside interference, believing this twisted growth is the true evolution of nature.",sp=0},{t="The Nightmare Made Flesh",b="Breaking the grip of the Druids of the Fang does not automatically save Naralex. When his remaining uncorrupted disciples initiate the ritual to gently rouse him from his trance at Dreamer's Rock, the slumbering elf's thrashing subconscious violently purges its deepest terror. The creature that erupts forth—a monstrous, distorted murloc named Mutanus the Devourer—is the physical manifestation of Naralex's worst nightmares. Only by slaying this abomination can the channel to the Nightmare be snapped, freeing Naralex to wake, assume avian form, and take flight from the tainted caves.",sp=1}},faq={{q="Why is it called the Wailing Caverns?",a="The cavern earns its name from the mournful, howling cries heard throughout the tunnels. These sounds are produced naturally when subterranean steam vents and high-pressure gusts of wind force their way through tight fissures in the limestone rock.",al={"why wailing caverns","name origin","why do they wail"},it="name"},{q="What caused the beasts inside to become 'deviate'?",a="When Naralex fell under the sway of the Emerald Nightmare, the tainted dream energies bled directly into the underground springs. Drinking and living in these contaminated waters mutated the natural raptors, crocolisks, and serpents into unnatural 'deviate' variants.",al={"deviate corruption","why are raptors mutate","deviate beasts origin"},it="threat",nx={11}},{q="Who are the Druids of the Fang?",a="They were once the devoted night elf and tauren acolytes of Naralex. Corrupted alongside him by the Nightmare, their minds shattered and twisted their druidic arts into worship of serpents and venom, adopting titles like Cobrahn, Pythas, and Anacondra.",al={"fang druids","druids of the fang lore","who is serpentis"},it="people"},{q="Why is the final boss a giant murloc named Mutanus?",a="Mutanus appears during the attempt to awaken Naralex. Its nature and connection to the sleeping druid are revealed as the ritual unfolds.",al={"why mutanus murloc","what is mutanus","final boss lore"},sp=1,it="target"},{q="What happens after Mutanus is defeated?",a="The disciple's attempt to awaken Naralex continues after the confrontation. The druid's fate is revealed at the end of the ritual.",al={"waking naralex","naralex ending","what happens to naralex"},sp=1,it="next_step"},{q="Who is living in the cave above the cavern entrance?",a="Perched inside the cavern's skull-like rock eye socket are Cenarion Circle loyalists, including Nalpak and Ebru. They seek brave travelers to harvest deviate hides and cleanse the corruption before it completely engulfs the Barrens.",al={"cave above entrance","snake skull eye npcs","who is nalpak and ebru"},it="residents"},{q="What is the Wailing Caverns?",a="The Wailing Caverns are an expansive underground cave network running beneath the arid Barrens, near the Lushwater Oasis. Its natural subterranean springs channel water for miles under the earth, feeding the rare surface oases scattered across the region. Discovered by the night elf druid Naralex, it was meant to be the heart of a grand project of natural regrowth. Instead, it became an epicenter of dangerous corruption after a tragic catastrophe took hold of the druids within.",al={"what is wailing caverns","wailing caverns overview","about wailing caverns"},it="place",add="3386ab3f"},{q="Who lives down there?",a="The caverns teem with unnatural wildlife and rogue druids. Naralex's corrupted followers, the Druids of the Fang, have claimed the tunnels as their domain alongside mutated serpents, oozes, raptors, and crocolisks. Outside the instance gate, wild beasts, oozes, and even outcasts lurk in the damp passages, while the corrupted druids guard the inner chambers and protect their sleeping master.",al={"who is in wailing caverns","wailing caverns creatures","inhabitants of wailing caverns"},it="residents",add="e070a543"},{q="Why did the Horde send me here?",a="The strange mutation of local beasts and the foul energies bubbling out of the Lushwater Oasis threaten the entire Barrens. The Horde and the Cenarion druids of Thunder Bluff cannot tolerate an uncontrolled dark power poisoning the land and waterways right on the doorstep of the Crossroads. You were sent to investigate, put an end to the rogue leaders of the Fang, and help quell the growing danger.",al={"why am i in wailing caverns","horde wailing caverns mission","why send me to wailing caverns"},it="arrival",add="49d47201"},{q="Is this part of a bigger problem in the Barrens?",a="Yes. The subterranean channels beneath these caves feed the surface oases across the Barrens. The Nightmare's taint corrupting the waters within the caverns has begun spilling out into the surrounding landscape, causing wild creatures like raptors and crocolisks to mutate and turning the Lushwater Oasis into a breeding ground for strange deviate life.",al={"barrens oasis problem","deviate corruption barrens","is wailing caverns affecting the barrens"},it="conflict",add="d445bb78"},{q="Are the deviates spreading outside the caverns?",a="They already are. The underground springs flow directly into surface oases like Lushwater, bringing unnatural growth and mutated creatures out into the open savannah. Strange creatures like Deviate Fish can be pulled from the waters outside, and aggressive mutated predators increasingly harass travelers between the oases and the Crossroads.",al={"are deviates spreading","deviate beasts barrens","deviate fish outside"},it="threat",add="038fd1cf"},{q="Who is in charge down here?",a="While Naralex lies trapped in his corrupted slumber deep within the caves, the daily rule of the caverns belongs to the Druids of the Fang. They are led by Lord Serpentis, once Naralex's finest student, who rallied his twisted brethren to remake the land into their own warped paradise alongside other fang lords like Cobrahn, Pythas, and Lady Anacondra.",al={"who leads wailing caverns","wailing caverns leader","boss of wailing caverns"},it="in_charge",add="8502642f"},{q="What is the Emerald Dream and how does it connect to this cave?",a="The Emerald Dream is a vast spirit realm representing Azeroth untouched and wild, stewarded by the green dragonflight and accessible to druids. Naralex believed he could channel the pure, restorative energies of the Dream into the underground aquifers of the Wailing Caverns to restore lush plant life to the Barrens. However, when he tapped into it, he was ensnared by the Emerald Nightmare, projecting a twisted version of nature into the physical caves.",al={"emerald dream connection","wailing caverns emerald dream","naralex emerald dream"},it="history",add="32be29c8"},{q="Why is everyone so worried about this place?",a="The subterranean springs in the caverns feed the primary oases that sustain life across the arid Barrens. If the Emerald Nightmare's taint continues to seep into those waterways unchecked, the twisted mutations and madness corrupting the cave's flora and fauna could spread across the entire region, turning the land into a waking horror.",al={"why worry about wailing caverns","wailing caverns threat to barrens","how bad is wailing caverns"},it="threat",add="38e519c2"},{q="How did I end up in Wailing Caverns?",a="You traveled south from the Crossroads into the Lushwater Oasis, following reports of bizarre beasts and corrupted waters bleeding through the Barrens. Tucked behind the lush foliage and Kolkar centaur camps sits a massive, skull-shaped cavern carved into the rock. Drawn by calls for aid from Thunder Bluff, Ratchet goblins seeking odd essences, or disciples camped in the skull's eye above, you descended past the winding fissures and hiss of underground geysers into the groaning depths below.",al={"how did i get here","how do i reach wailing caverns","where did i come from to get here"},it="arrival",add="81917ac6"},{q="What am I supposed to be doing in Wailing Caverns?",a="You are here to purge the corruption that has gripped this underground spring. The night elf druid Naralex fell into a nightmarish slumber trying to revitalize the Barrens, twisting the creatures within and driving his disciples into the venomous Druids of the Fang. You must hunt down the four Fanglords—Lady Anacondra, Lord Cobrahn, Lord Pythas, and Lord Serpentis—to break their grip, and then help the remaining disciple awaken Naralex before his fevered nightmare consumes the oasis completely.",al={"what is my goal here","why am i in wailing caverns","what am i doing down here"},it="purpose",add="28a012f3"}},ang={["class:Druid"]="For druids of both Cenarion tradition and the tauren walk, the caverns are a tragic warning of the perils within the Emerald Dream and a solemn duty to purge their fallen brethren, the Druids of the Fang.",["race:Tauren"]="The twisted waters threaten the fragile oases that sustain life across the Barrens, making the cleansing of the springs vital to the tribes of Mulgore and the Crossroads.",["race:NightElf"]="Naralex was a revered figure among night elf druids, and the tragedy of his corruption by the Emerald Nightmare represents a painful catastrophe for his kin across the sea."},kw={"deviate","druids of the fang","emerald nightmare","lady anacondra","lord cobrahn","lord pythas","lord serpentis","lushwater oasis","mutanus","naralex","verdan"},rel={"npc:naralex","topic:druids-of-the-fang","npc:mutanus-the-devourer","quest:914","subzone:lushwater-oasis","topic:emerald-dream","npc:lord-serpentis","zone:barrens"},m={levels="17-24"},src={"Wailing Caverns"}}
